argets own.\n.skilled/commands/doctor/sk-skill.md:10:This command is a thin router. It binds the read-only `check` target or the mutating `convert` target from `_routes.yaml`, then loads that target's workflow YAML and the presentation contract.\n.skilled/commands/doctor/sk-skill.md:65:4. Resolve `yaml`, `setup_vars`, `allowed_flags`, `mutating` and script invocations from the route, and reject a flag outside its `allowed_flags`, including a flag the other target owns.\n.skilled/commands/doctor/install.md:59:3. Resolve `yaml`, `setup_vars`, `allowed_flags`, `mutating` and script invocations from the route, and reject a flag outside its `allowed_flags`. The class column of a printed step is the owning route's `mutating` value, verbatim.\n.skilled/commands/doctor/skill-advisor.md:69:5. Resolve `yaml`, `setup_vars`, `allowed_flags`, `mutating`, `mcp_tools`, `cli_commands`, and script invocations from the route.\n.skilled/commands/doctor/symlink.md:71:4. Resolve `yaml`, `setup_vars`, `allowed_flags`, `mutating` and script invocations from the route, and reject a flag outside its `allowed_flags`, including a flag the other targets own.\n.skilled/commands/doctor/git.md:67:4. Resolve `yaml`, `setup_vars`, `allowed_flags`, `mutating`, `mcp_tools`, and script invocations from the route.\n.skilled/commands/doctor/ci.md:67:4. Resolve `yaml`, `setup_vars`, `allowed_flags`, `mutating` and the script invocations from the route.\n.skilled/commands/speckit/save.md:53:- Default mode returns the save plan without mutating.\n.skilled/commands/speckit/save.md:86:5. In default mode, return the save plan without mutating.\n.skilled/commands/speckit/save.md:139:The router resolves and validates the target spec folder, extracts the session context, chooses a route category, and either returns a non-mutating save plan (default) or runs the metadata/description/graph-metadata refresh via `generate-context.js` (explicit apply/full-auto). A full-auto run also writes the continuity fields and any operator decisions.\n.skilled/commands/create/skill-parent.md:82:Both workflows classify the target's root `ROUTER.md` on `update` and emit exactly one action line before mutating anything:\n=== derive: policy/mutating ===\n51:// silent fallthrough would hand a mutating command the read-only policy (or the\n183:        mutating: entry.mutating,\n454:// The policy ladder reads only these keys, so a wrong value has to fail here\n457:  if (!MUTATING_CLASSES.includes(record.mutating)) {\n459:      `[command-bridges] ${label} has mutating ${JSON.stringify(record.mutating)}; `\n485:// One policy per command, decided from the risk keys alone so the answer never\n492:  if (record.doctor === true && record.mutating === 'mutates') return 'ask';\n493:  if (record.mutating === 'read-only') return 'run';\n494:  if (record.mutating === 'add-only' && record.write_scope === 'spec-folder') return 'run';\n501:// its writes land before its policy may be derived.\n523:        mutating: entry.mutating,\n551:      mutating: fields.mutating,\n568:      mutating: route.mutating,\n582:      mutating: item?.mutating,\n603:          mutating: entry?.mutating,\n613:      mutating: item.mutating,\n654:      mutating: record.mutating,\n656:      policy: derivePolicy(record),\n720:// question; add-only and mutating routes keep the read-only confidence floor.\n722:  return item.mutating === 'read-only';\n760:    mutating: item.mutating,\n1120:// whole record comes back because the class travels with the policy it justifies.\n1127:    throw new Error(`[command-bridges] No policy record for ${runnable}`);\n1132:      throw new Error(`[command-bridges] No policy record for ${runnable}`);\n1139:    POLICY_STRICTNESS.indexOf(record.policy) > POLICY_STRICTNESS.indexOf(strictest.policy)\n1156:    const policyRecord = runnablePolicyRecord(runnable, policies);\n1157:    runnablePolicies.set(runnable, policyRecord.policy);\n1163:      policy: policyRecord.policy,\n1164:      // The class travels with the policy that justifies it, so a record that\n1166:      ...(policyRecord.mutating ? { mutating: policyRecord.mutating } : {}),\n1178:  // reader can type a command no scorer offers and still needs its policy and its\n1183:    const policy = runnablePolicyRecord(runnable, policies).policy;\n1185:    if (previous && (previous.policy !== policy || previous.ownerSkillId !== entry.skillId)) {\n1189:      policy,\n1199:        `policy: ${tsString(row.policy)}`,\n1201:      if (row.mutating) fields.push(`mutating: ${tsString(row.mutating)}`);\n1205:  const policyLines = [...runnablePolicies.entries()]\n1207:    .map(([runnable, policy]) => `  ${tsString(runnable)}: ${tsString(policy)},`);\n1211:      `  ${tsString(runnable)}: { policy: ${tsString(row.policy)}, `\n1219:    ...policyLines,\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/commands/design/extract.md:109:Confirm source and overwrite policy, run the owned extract-write-validate pipeline, capture provenance and coverage, label inference and gaps, and return the validated artifact path. This is the only mutating design mode, and it mutates only through its owned pipeline. Never silently chains or invokes a sibling command.\n.skilled/commands/doctor/helper.md:40:- The class shown on every line is the manifest's `mutating` value for that route, verbatim, so `/doctor:env list` reads `mutates` and a read-only route reads `read-only`.\n.skilled/commands/doctor/helper.md:61:3. Resolve `yaml`, `setup_vars`, `allowed_flags`, `mutating` and script invocations from the route, and reject a flag outside its `allowed_flags`.\n.skilled/commands/doctor/sk-code.md:59:4. Resolve `yaml`, `setup_vars`, `allowed_flags`, `mutating` and script invocations from the route, and reject a flag outside its `allowed_flags`.\n.skilled/commands/doctor/speckit.md:52:3. Resolve `yaml`, `setup_vars`, `allowed_flags`, `mutating`, `mcp_tools`, and script invocation