{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794550395945,"sessionID":"ses_e2c7999e1ffeYcD6BDSYeMhQPJ","part":{"partID":"prt_1d389f24b0010Go6WpXoKo9k4a","sessionID":"ses_e2c7999e1ffeYcD6BDSYeMhQPJ","messageID":"msg_1d389cdaa001Mi2ghEtsx2Vj2f","type":"tool","id":"call_d7428ace6a164633b9dc8424","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research; sed -n '620,700p' .skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml; echo \"=== install.md head ===\"; sed -n '1,60p' .skilled/commands/doctor/install.md"},"output":"      - 'node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs unlink --run <dir> --yes  # removes the recorded links and empty folders and the recorded ignore lines; the workflow passes --yes only after its own yes'\n    trigger_phrases:\n      - \"undo a skilled symlink run\"\n      - \"remove the skilled symlinks again\"\n      - \"unlink skilled from my project\"\n\n  - command: /doctor:install\n    target: guide\n    yaml: doctor-install.yaml\n    setup_vars: [execution_mode, root, runtimes, json_output]\n    allowed_flags: [\"--json\", \"--root <dir>\", \"--runtimes <list>\"]\n    mutating: read-only\n    gate3_location: \"n/a (read-only guide; it checks the two builds, runs the symlink engine's check once and prints the ordered writing commands for the operator to run)\"\n    mcp_tools: []   # script-only; no MCP calls\n    script_invocations:\n      - 'test -d .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist  # the spec-kit build the session hooks load'\n      - 'node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs list-tools --format json  # the advisor build; exit 0 means built'\n      - 'node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs check --root <dir>  # the workflow adds --runtimes and --link-instructions only when the operator chose them'\n    trigger_phrases:\n      - \"install skilled into my project\"\n      - \"set up skilled in another repo\"\n      - \"use skilled in my own project\"\n      - \"onboard a project repo to skilled\"\n      - \"guide me through installing skilled\"\n      - \"walk me through a first install of skilled\"\n      - \"first install of skilled in my project\"\n      - \"skilled in my other repository\"\n      - \"skilled in another repository\"\n\n  - command: /doctor:overlay\n    target: status\n    default_target: true\n    yaml: doctor-overlay-status.yaml\n    setup_vars: [execution_mode, root, json_output, audit_output]\n    allowed_flags: [\"--json\", \"--audit\", \"--root <dir>\"]\n    mutating: read-only\n    gate3_location: \"n/a (read-only diagnostic; the engine classifies every overlay destination in the vendored tree, runs the overlay manifest's read-only verify checks and writes nothing)\"\n    mcp_tools: []   # script-only; no MCP calls\n    script_invocations:\n      - 'node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs status  # exit 0 = in sync, 1 = something out of sync, 2 = a failed precondition; the workflow adds --root <dir>, --json and --audit only when the operator passed them, and --audit prints one AUDIT line per unowned path that differs from upstream at the pin, is missing from the tree or is tracked there and never upstream, then the audit count. A finding fails the status'\n    trigger_phrases:\n      - \"check my vendored skilled overlays\"\n      - \"are my skilled overlays in sync\"\n      - \"which overlay destinations are out of sync\"\n      - \"vendored skilled overlay status\"\n      - \"does my vendored skilled tree still carry its overlays\"\n      - \"vendored skilled overlays out of sync\"\n      - \"does my vendored skilled copy still carry its overlays\"\n      - \"adopt the skilled overlay engine in my project\"\n      - \"migrate my own overlay folder to doctor overlay\"\n      - \"check whether my overlay sources sit on their layout path\"\n      - \"audit my vendored skilled tree for unowned files\"\n      - \"which root files my overlays own drifted upstream at the pinned commit\"\n      - \"we copy skilled into our repo and lose our edits on update\"\n      - \"agents overlay stale after a re-pin\"\n      - \"which overlay do I rebase\"\n      - \"rebase the overlay\"\n\n  - command: /doctor:overlay\n    target: apply\n    yaml: doctor-overlay-apply.yaml\n    setup_vars: [execution_mode, root, capture_path, adopt_path, relayout]\n    allowed_flags: [\"--root <dir>\", \"--capture <path>\", \"--adopt <path>\", \"--relayout\"]\n    mutating: mutates\n    gate3_location: \"the overlay destinations and layout links the overlay manifest names inside the vendored tree, the outputs of the manifest's regenerate steps, and <overlay folder>/sync-state.json, all under the engine's own <overlay folder>/.build-lock; with --capture <path>, only the one overlay source that path maps to plus sync-state.json; with --adopt <path>, the copy of that vendored path in the overlay folder and one new entry in <overlay folder>/overlay-manifest.json, followed by the same apply; with --relayout, the overlay sources the manifest keeps off their layout paths, moved inside the overlay folder to the same path with the leading dot dropped, the layout-link targets that reach them, the source, fragment and base fields of <overlay folder>/overlay-manifest.json, and the backup in <overlay folder>/relayout-runs/<stamp>/, followed by the same apply; the write runs only after the operator approved the status report this run printed, or the LAYOUT lines in it when --relayout carries the run\"\n    mcp_tools: []   # script-only; no MCP calls\n    script_invocations:\n      - 'node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs status  # read-only: the report the run shows as its plan before the question, and the re-read after the write'\n      - 'node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs apply  # applies every overlay under the engine lock, then regenerates and verifies; writes nothing while a destination is live-edited, both-changed or upstream-moved; run only after the apply yes'\n      - 'node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs apply --capture <path>  # moves one live edit into its overlay source; run only after the capture yes'\n      - 'node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs apply --adopt <path>  # copies one unowned vendored path into the overlay folder, appends its manifest entry and applies; exit 0 = adopted and applied, 1 = the apply was blocked, 2 = a refusal with nothing written; run only after the adopt yes'\n      - 'node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs apply --relayout  # moves every off-layout copy onto its layout path under the engine lock, backs up what it leaves in relayout-runs/, points the manifest fields and layout links there, retargets each live link that named a moved copy with its relinked line, and prints one moved line per path, then names the apply that follows; exit 0 = done, 2 = a refusal with nothing written, such as a target that already exists; run only after the relayout yes, followed by apply'\n    trigger_phrases:\n      - \"apply the skilled overlays\"\n      - \"put my overlays back into vendored skilled\"\n      - \"capture a live edit into its overlay\"\n      - \"reapply overlays after copying skilled\"\n      - \"apply the overlays back onto the vendored copy\"\n      - \"put the overlays back on vendored skilled\"\n      - \"move my overlay sources onto the layout folder\"\n      - \"take over the overlay lock a dead run left behind\"\n=== install.md head ===\n---\ndescription: \"Get the ordered steps that put Skilled into your own project repo, ready to run.\"\nargument-hint: \"[--root <dir>] [--runtimes <list>] [--json] | list | ?\"\nallowed-tools: Read, Bash\n---\n<!-- skill_agent: system-skilled-doctor -->\n\n# /doctor:install Router\n\nThis command is a thin router. It binds the read-only `guide` target from `_routes.yaml`, then loads that target's workflow YAML and the presentation contract. It writes nothing. Every step that writes is printed for the operator to run.\n\n## 1. ROUTER CONTRACT\n\nDo not dispatch agents from this Markdown file. Do not edit workflow YAML while executing this command.\n\nLoad the presentation contract before showing the build check, the install prompt, the symlink check, the ordered steps, the caveat line or next-step text.\n\nThis command never runs a target that writes, and never adds an argument to a printed command beyond the values the operator gave: `--root`, `--runtimes`, the link shape and the instruction choice.\n\n---\n\n## 2. OWNED ASSETS\n\n| Purpose | Asset |\n|---------|-------|\n| Route manifest | `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml` |\n| Presentation source of truth | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt` |\n| Symlink engine | `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs` |\n\n---\n\n## 3. MODE ROUTING\n\n- `_routes.yaml` is the canonical routing and mutation-class manifest, and this command owns the route whose `command` is `/doctor:install`.\n- `execution_mode` is always `INTERACTIVE`. No `:auto` or `:confirm` suffix is supported.\n- The route's target is `guide` and it is never typed: `/doctor:install` alone binds it. A second positional token is an argument failure.\n- `--root <dir>` is the target repo's absolute path. `--runtimes <list>` is a comma list drawn from `claude`, `opencode`, `codex`, `cursor`, `devin` and `pi`; without it the engine keeps the runtimes its own detection finds in the root. `--json` prints one JSON object and nothing else.\n- `list`, `?` and `menu` as the whole argument print the ordered steps from the presentation and stop, so no workflow loads and nothing is inspected.\n- The link shape and the instruction choice have no flag, so both are always answered at the prompt. A `--root` or `--runtimes` already passed drops its own question and nothing else.\n- The YAML owns workflow behavior; the presentation text owns visible wording and layout.\n\n---\n\n## 4. EXECUTION TARGETS\n\n| Target | Workflow |\n|--------|----------|\n| `guide` | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install.yaml` |\n\n| Argument | Applies to | Effect |\n|----------|------------|--------|\n| `--root <dir>` | `guide` | The project repo to inspect and to print the steps for |\n| `--runtimes <list>` | `guide` | Comma list of runtime folders to link; absent, the ones already in the root |\n| `--json` | `guide` | Print one JSON object and nothing else |\n| `list`, `?`, `menu` | the command | Print the ordered steps, and load no workflow |\n\n1. Read `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt`.\n2. Read `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml` and keep the `/doctor:install` route, plus the route that owns each command the checklist prints.\n3. Resolve `yaml`, `setup_vars`, `allowed_flags`, `mutating` and script invocations from the route, and reject a flag outside its `allowed_flags`. The class column of a printed step is the owning route's `mutating` value, verbatim.\n4. Load the resolved workflow YAML from `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/<yaml>` and execute it step by step.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"      - 'node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs unlink --run <dir> --yes  # removes the recorded links and empty folders and the recorded ignore lines; the workflow passes --yes only after its own yes'\n    trigger_phrases:\n      - \"undo a skilled symlink run\"\n      - \"remove the skilled symlinks again\"\n      - \"unlink skilled from my project\"\n\n  - command: /doctor:install\n    target: guide\n    yaml: doctor-install.yaml\n    setup_vars: [execution_mode, root, runtimes, json_output]\n    allowed_flags: [\"--json\", \"--root <dir>\", \"--runtimes <list>\"]\n    mutating: read-only\n    gate3_location: \"n/a (read-only guide; it checks the two builds, runs the symlink engine's check once and prints the ordered writing commands for the operator to run)\"\n    mcp_tools: []   # script-only; no MCP calls\n    script_invocations:\n      - 'test -d .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist  # the spec-kit build the session hooks load'\n      - 'node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs list-tools --format json  # the advisor build; exit 0 means built'\n      - 'node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs check --root <dir>  # the workflow adds --runtimes and --link-instructions only when the operator chose them'\n    trigger_phrases:\n      - \"install skilled into my project\"\n      - \"set up skilled in another repo\"\n      - \"use skilled in my own project\"\n      - \"onboard a project repo to skilled\"\n      - \"guide me through installing skilled\"\n      - \"walk me through a first install of skilled\"\n      - \"first install of skilled in my project\"\n      - \"skilled in my other repository\"\n      - \"skilled in another repository\"\n\n  - command: /doctor:overlay\n    target: status\n    default_target: true\n    yaml: doctor-overlay-status.yaml\n    setup_vars: [execution_mode, root, json_output, audit_output]\n    allowed_flags: [\"--json\", \"--audit\", \"--root <dir>\"]\n    mutating: read-only\n    gate3_location: \"n/a (read-only diagnostic; the engine classifies every overlay destination in the vendored tree, runs the overlay manifest's read-only verify checks and writes nothing)\"\n    mcp_tools: []   # script-only; no MCP calls\n    script_invocations:\n      - 'node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs status  # exit 0 = in sync, 1 = something out of sync, 2 = a failed precondition; the workflow adds --root <dir>, --json and --audit only when the operator passed them, and --audit prints one AUDIT line per unowned path that differs from upstream at the pin, is missing from the tree or is tracked there and never upstream, then the audit count. A finding fails the status'\n    trigger_phrases:\n      - \"check my vendored skilled overlays\"\n      - \"are my skilled overlays in sync\"\n      - \"which overlay destinations are out of sync\"\n      - \"vendored skilled overlay status\"\n      - \"does my vendored skilled tree still carry its overlays\"\n      - \"vendored skilled overlays out of sync\"\n      - \"does my vendored skilled copy still carry its overlays\"\n      - \"adopt the skilled overlay engine in my project\"\n      - \"migrate my own overlay folder to doctor overlay\"\n      - \"check whether my overlay sources sit on their layout path\"\n      - \"audit my vendored skilled tree for unowned files\"\n      - \"which root files my overlays own drifted upstream at the pinned commit\"\n      - \"we copy skilled into our repo and lose our edits on update\"\n      - \"agents overlay stale after a re-pin\"\n      - \"which overlay do I rebase\"\n      - \"rebase the overlay\"\n\n  - command: /doctor:overlay\n    target: apply\n    yaml: doctor-overlay-apply.yaml\n    setup_vars: [execution_mode, root, capture_path, adopt_path, relayout]\n    allowed_flags: [\"--root <dir>\", \"--capture <path>\", \"--adopt <path>\", \"--relayout\"]\n    mutating: mutates\n    gate3_location: \"the overlay destinations and layout links the overlay manifest names inside the vendored tree, the outputs of the manifest's regenerate steps, and <overlay folder>/sync-state.json, all under the engine's own <overlay folder>/.build-lock; with --capture <path>, only the one overlay source that path maps to plus sync-state.json; with --adopt <path>, the copy of that vendored path in the overlay folder and one new entry in <overlay folder>/overlay-manifest.json, followed by the same apply; with --relayout, the overlay sources the manifest keeps off their layout paths, moved inside the overlay folder to the same path with the leading dot dropped, the layout-link targets that reach them, the source, fragment and base fields of <overlay folder>/overlay-manifest.json, and the backup in <overlay folder>/relayout-runs/<stamp>/, followed by the same apply; the write runs only after the operator approved the status report this run printed, or the LAYOUT lines in it when --relayout carries the run\"\n    mcp_tools: []   # script-only; no MCP calls\n    script_invocations:\n      - 'node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs status  # read-only: the report the run shows as its plan before the question, and the re-read after the write'\n      - 'node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs apply  # applies every overlay under the engine lock, then regenerates and verifies; writes nothing while a destination is live-edited, both-changed or upstream-moved; run only after the apply yes'\n      - 'node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs apply --capture <path>  # moves one live edit into its overlay source; run only after the capture yes'\n      - 'node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs apply --adopt <path>  # copies one unowned vendored path into the overlay folder, appends its manifest entry and applies; exit 0 = adopted and applied, 1 = the apply was blocked, 2 = a refusal with nothing written; run only after the adopt yes'\n      - 'node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs apply --relayout  # moves every off-layout copy onto its layout path under the engine lock, backs up what it leaves in relayout-runs/, points the manifest fields and layout links there, retargets each live link that named a moved copy with its relinked line, and prints one moved line per path, then names the apply that follows; exit 0 = done, 2 = a refusal with nothing written, such as a target that already exists; run only after the relayout yes, followed by apply'\n    trigger_phrases:\n      - \"apply the skilled overlays\"\n      - \"put my overlays back into vendored skilled\"\n      - \"capture a live edit into its overlay\"\n      - \"reapply overlays after copying skilled\"\n      - \"apply the overlays back onto the vendored copy\"\n      - \"put the overlays back on vendored skilled\"\n      - \"move my overlay sources onto the layout folder\"\n      - \"take over the overlay lock a dead run left behind\"\n=== install.md head ===\n---\ndescription: \"Get the ordered steps that put Skilled into your own project repo, ready to run.\"\nargument-hint: \"[--root <dir>] [--runtimes <list>] [--json] | list | ?\"\nallowed-tools: Read, Bash\n---\n<!-- skill_agent: system-skilled-doctor -->\n\n# /doctor:install Router\n\nThis command is a thin router. It binds the read-only `guide` target from `_routes.yaml`, then loads that target's workflow YAML and the presentation contract. It writes nothing. Every step that writes is printed for the operator to run.\n\n## 1. ROUTER CONTRACT\n\nDo not dispatch agents from this Markdown file. Do not edit workflow YAML while executing this command.\n\nLoad the presentation contract before showing the build check, the install prompt, the symlink check, the ordered steps, the caveat line or next-step text.\n\nThis command never runs a target that writes, and never adds an argument to a printed command beyond the values the operator gave: `--root`, `--runtimes`, the link shape and the instruction choice.\n\n---\n\n## 2. OWNED ASSETS\n\n| Purpose | Asset |\n|---------|-------|\n| Route manifest | `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml` |\n| Presentation source of truth | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt` |\n| Symlink engine | `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs` |\n\n---\n\n## 3. MODE ROUTING\n\n- `_routes.yaml` is the canonical routing and mutation-class manifest, and this command owns the route whose `command` is `/doctor:install`.\n- `execution_mode` is always `INTERACTIVE`. No `:auto` or `:confirm` suffix is supported.\n- The route's target is `guide` and it is never typed: `/doctor:install` alone binds it. A second positional token is an argument failure.\n- `--root <dir>` is the target repo's absolute path. `--runtimes <list>` is a comma list drawn from `claude`, `opencode`, `codex`, `cursor`, `devin` and `pi`; without it the engine keeps the runtimes its own detection finds in the root. `--json` prints one JSON object and nothing else.\n- `list`, `?` and `menu` as the whole argument print the ordered steps from the presentation and stop, so no workflow loads and nothing is inspected.\n- The link shape and the instruction choice have no flag, so both are always answered at the prompt. A `--root` or `--runtimes` already passed drops its own question and nothing else.\n- The YAML owns workflow behavior; the presentation text owns visible wording and layout.\n\n---\n\n## 4. EXECUTION TARGETS\n\n| Target | Workflow |\n|--------|----------|\n| `guide` | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install.yaml` |\n\n| Argument | Applies to | Effect |\n|----------|------------|--------|\n| `--root <dir>` | `guide` | The project repo to inspect and to print the steps for |\n| `--runtimes <list>` | `guide` | Comma list of runtime folders to link; absent, the ones already in the root |\n| `--json` | `guide` | Print one JSON object and nothing else |\n| `list`, `?`, `menu` | the command | Print the ordered steps, and load no workflow |\n\n1. Read `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt`.\n2. Read `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml` and keep the `/doctor:install` route, plus the route that owns each command the checklist prints.\n3. Resolve `yaml`, `setup_vars`, `allowed_flags`, `mutating` and script invocations from the route, and reject a flag outside its `allowed_flags`. The class column of a printed step is the owning route's `mutating` value, verbatim.\n4. Load the resolved workflow YAML from `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/<yaml>` and execute it step by step.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research; sed -n '620,700p' 