{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794550451275,"sessionID":"ses_e2c7999e1ffeYcD6BDSYeMhQPJ","part":{"partID":"prt_1d38aca0300129oQpeBeiqNhjV","sessionID":"ses_e2c7999e1ffeYcD6BDSYeMhQPJ","messageID":"msg_1d38aa55d0018vI3LUs2lhON6g","type":"tool","id":"call_26f2cf8e98464304931a3022","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md"},"output":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md, lines 1-79\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Command Meaning Matching\"\n3: description: \"A command row can pass on meaning when the prompt's real embedding sits close to the row's own vector, so a paraphrase that shares no words with a command can still reach it.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"command meaning matching\"\n6:   - \"command row embedding\"\n7:   - \"vec_cmd table\"\n8:   - \"command meaning anchor\"\n9: version: 1.0.0.0\n10: ---\n11: \n12: # Command Meaning Matching\n13: \n14: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n15: \n16: A command row can pass on meaning when the prompt's real embedding sits close to the row's own vector, so a paraphrase that shares no words with a command can still reach it.\n17: \n18: A command row used to pass only on one of its own phrases or its slash string. A paraphrase shares none of those words, so it reached nothing. Meaning matching adds a second way in. It works only when the local embedder runs. Without it the advisor returns the phrase-only result.\n19: \n20: ---\n21: \n22: ## 2. HOW IT WORKS\n23: \n24: ### Command Vectors\n25: \n26: `derive-command-bridges.cjs` writes an `embeddingText` for each command row the TypeScript scorer serves, 45 rows in all. A metadata row leads with its `userIntent.job` sentence and adds its owned phrases. The `description` stands in only when the record states no job. A doctor row uses its router's frontmatter `description` and the route's trigger phrases. Slash command strings are stripped from the text.\n27: \n28: `skill_graph_scan` embeds that text into a separate `vec_cmd_<dim>` table. The table carries no foreign key, and the skill vector table is left untouched. A row whose text hash has not changed is skipped. A stored row that the deriver no longer generates is pruned.\n29: \n30: ### Passing on Meaning\n31: \n32: `requireCommandPhraseAnchor` in `fusion.ts` keeps a command row passing when it matched its own phrase. A row with no phrase match can still pass when the semantic lane reports a real embedder cosine of at least `COMMAND_MEANING_MIN_COSINE` (0.72). It must also lead the strongest other command row by `COMMAND_MEANING_MARGIN` (0.02). The row is then lifted to the confidence threshold and marked as a meaning pass. The word-overlap stand-in used under test reports its score differently, and it never counts.\n33: \n34: ### Eligibility\n35: \n36: A meaning pass lifts a command past the read-only confidence floor, so `commandMeaningEligible` asks the question that floor asks of a phrase match. A prompt matching `NO_EDIT_REQUEST`, such as \"no edits\", \"do not change\", \"just show\" or \"just list\", rules out every command on meaning. A read-only explainer prompt admits only a command marked `readOnly`, because running it is the answer. `readOnlyRouteAllowed` reads the same pattern, so the two gates cannot drift apart.\n37: \n38: ### Ranking\n39: \n40: `rankMeaningPassedCommandFirst` moves the best meaning-passed command to first place only when its cosine leads the top passing skill's cosine by the same 0.02. Otherwise the skill keeps its place and the command follows it.\n41: \n42: ### Measuring It\n43: \n44: `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs --real-embedding` scores the command corpus against this machine's skill graph and live embedder. It first checks that the embedder serves `nomic-embed-text` and that a `vec_cmd_*` table holds vectors, and it refuses `--write`. The committed baseline still comes from the fixture run, which has no real cosine.\n45: \n46: ---\n47: \n48: ## 3. SOURCE FILES\n49: \n50: ### Implementation\n51: \n52: | File | Layer | Role |\n53: |---|---|---|\n54: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs` | Script | Builds each row's `embeddingText` |\n55: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/command-bridges.generated.json` | Generated | Carries `embeddingText` per TypeScript-served row |\n56: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/embedders/schema.ts` | Shared | Names and creates the `vec_cmd_<dim>` table |\n57: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/skill-graph/skill-graph-db.ts` | Shared | Embeds, skips and prunes command vectors during a scan |\n58: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts` | Shared | Meaning pass, its two bars, eligibility and the ranking rule |\n59: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs` | Script | The `--real-embedding` measurement |\n60: \n61: ### Validation And Tests\n62: \n63: | File | Type | Role |\n64: |---|---|---|\n65: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts` | Vitest | 17 cases: cosine bar, margin, stand-in refusal, eligibility and ranking rule |\n66: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-bridges-drift-guard.vitest.ts` | Vitest | Generated bridge file matches the deriver |\n67: \n68: ---\n69: \n70: ## 4. SOURCE METADATA\n71: \n72: - Group: Scorer fusion\n73: - Canonical catalog source: `feature-catalog.md`\n74: - Feature file path: `scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md`\n75: \n76: Related references:\n77: \n78: - [doctor-command-routing.md](./doctor-command-routing.md) - The phrase anchor that command rows pass on by default.\n79: - [five-lane-fusion.md](./five-lane-fusion.md) - The semantic lane that supplies the cosine.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md, lines 1-79\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Command Meaning Matching\"\n3: description: \"A command row can pass on meaning when the prompt's real embedding sits close to the row's own vector, so a paraphrase that shares no words with a command can still reach it.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"command meaning matching\"\n6:   - \"command row embedding\"\n7:   - \"vec_cmd table\"\n8:   - \"command meaning anchor\"\n9: version: 1.0.0.0\n10: ---\n11: \n12: # Command Meaning Matching\n13: \n14: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n15: \n16: A command row can pass on meaning when the prompt's real embedding sits close to the row's own vector, so a paraphrase that shares no words with a command can still reach it.\n17: \n18: A command row used to pass only on one of its own phrases or its slash string. A paraphrase shares none of those words, so it reached nothing. Meaning matching adds a second way in. It works only when the local embedder runs. Without it the advisor returns the phrase-only result.\n19: \n20: ---\n21: \n22: ## 2. HOW IT WORKS\n23: \n24: ### Command Vectors\n25: \n26: `derive-command-bridges.cjs` writes an `embeddingText` for each command row the TypeScript scorer serves, 45 rows in all. A metadata row leads with its `userIntent.job` sentence and adds its owned phrases. The `description` stands in only when the record states no job. A doctor row uses its router's frontmatter `description` and the route's trigger phrases. Slash command strings are stripped from the text.\n27: \n28: `skill_graph_scan` embeds that text into a separate `vec_cmd_<dim>` table. The table carries no foreign key, and the skill vector table is left untouched. A row whose text hash has not changed is skipped. A stored row that the deriver no longer generates is pruned.\n29: \n30: ### Passing on Meaning\n31: \n32: `requireCommandPhraseAnchor` in `fusion.ts` keeps a command row passing when it matched its own phrase. A row with no phrase match can still pass when the semantic lane reports a real embedder cosine of at least `COMMAND_MEANING_MIN_COSINE` (0.72). It must also lead the strongest other command row by `COMMAND_MEANING_MARGIN` (0.02). The row is then lifted to the confidence threshold and marked as a meaning pass. The word-overlap stand-in used under test reports its score differently, and it never counts.\n33: \n34: ### Eligibility\n35: \n36: A meaning pass lifts a command past the read-only confidence floor, so `commandMeaningEligible` asks the question that floor asks of a phrase match. A prompt matching `NO_EDIT_REQUEST`, such as \"no edits\", \"do not change\", \"just show\" or \"just list\", rules out every command on meaning. A read-only explainer prompt admits only a command marked `readOnly`, because running it is the answer. `readOnlyRouteAllowed` reads the same pattern, so the two gates cannot drift apart.\n37: \n38: ### Ranking\n39: \n40: `rankMeaningPassedCommandFirst` moves the best meaning-passed command to first place only when its cosine leads the top passing skill's cosine by the same 0.02. Otherwise the skill keeps its place and the command follows it.\n41: \n42: ### Measuring It\n43: \n44: `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs --real-embedding` scores the command corpus against this machine's skill graph and live embedder. It first checks that the embedder serves `nomic-embed-text` and that a `vec_cmd_*` table holds vectors, and it refuses `--write`. The committed baseline still comes from the fixture run, which has no real cosine.\n45: \n46: ---\n47: \n48: ## 3. SOURCE FILES\n49: \n50: ### Implementation\n51: \n52: | File | Layer | Role |\n53: |---|---|---|\n54: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs` | Script | Builds each row's `embeddingText` |\n55: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/command-bridges.generated.json` | Generated | Carries `embeddingText` per TypeScript-served row |\n56: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/embedders/schema.ts` | Shared | Names and creates the `vec_cmd_<dim>` table |\n57: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/skill-graph/skill-graph-db.ts` | Shared | Embeds, skips and prunes command vectors during a scan |\n58: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts` | Shared | Meaning pass, its two bars, eligibility and the ranking rule |\n59: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs` | Script | The `--real-embedding` measurement |\n60: \n61: ### Validation And Tests\n62: \n63: | File | Type | Role |\n64: |---|---|---|\n65: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts` | Vitest | 17 cases: cosine bar, margin, stand-in refusal, eligibility and ranking rule |\n66: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-bridges-drift-guard.vitest.ts` | Vitest | Generated bridge file matches the deriver |\n67: \n68: ---\n69: \n70: ## 4. SOURCE METADATA\n71: \n72: - Group: Scorer fusion\n73: - Canonical catalog source: `feature-catalog.md`\n74: - Feature file path: `scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md`\n75: \n76: Related references:\n77: \n78: - [doctor-command-routing.md](./doctor-command-routing.md) - The phrase anchor that command rows pass on by default.\n79: - [five-lane-fusion.md](./five-lane-fusion.md) - The semantic lane that supplies the cosine."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794550450691,"end":1794550451275}}}}
