{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794550919841,"sessionID":"ses_e2c7999e1ffeYcD6BDSYeMhQPJ","part":{"partID":"prt_1d391f004002y4pNp33UeQzBuW","sessionID":"ses_e2c7999e1ffeYcD6BDSYeMhQPJ","messageID":"msg_1d39182a3001QyNNAHmJqE4hWT","type":"tool","id":"call_1645290cb31c4506aa8bde24","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research; grep -n \"command\\|45\\|46\\|attach\\|policy\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/README.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/scorer/README.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md | head -50"},"output":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/README.md:16:`lib/scorer/` contains the native scoring modules used by the skill advisor to rank candidate skills. It combines lane-specific evidence, text matching, age policy, ambiguity handling, explicit alias canonicalization, fusion and output projection into prompt-safe recommendation scores.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/README.md:22:- Canonicalizes narrow command/skill alias groups before campaign scoring compares expected and actual routes.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/README.md:32:+-- age-policy.ts            # Age-aware ranking policy\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/README.md:33:+-- aliases.ts               # Narrow command/skill alias canonicalization\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/README.md:55:| `fusion.ts` | Combines lane scores into final advisor ranking signals through RRF fusion, with a conflict-match rerank seam and a self-recommendation guard that penalizes advisor self-recommendations. `requireCommandPhraseAnchor` keeps a passing command row passing only when the explicit-author lane matched one of its own phrases or its slash string, or when it passes on meaning: a real embedder cosine of at least `COMMAND_MEANING_MIN_COSINE` (0.72) with a lead of `COMMAND_MEANING_MARGIN` (0.02) over the next command row. The word-overlap stand-in used under test never counts. `commandMeaningEligible` decides who may pass on meaning: a prompt matching `NO_EDIT_REQUEST`, the pattern `readOnlyRouteAllowed` also reads, rules out every command, and a read-only explainer admits only a command whose route only reads. `rankMeaningPassedCommandFirst` moves a meaning-passed command ahead of the top passing skill only when its cosine leads that skill's by the same margin. |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/README.md:57:| `aliases.ts` | Canonicalizes explicit command/skill alias groups for route comparisons. |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/README.md:59:| `ambiguity.ts` | Detects close or unclear recommendation states. A command row and its `ownerSkill` count as one answer, so they never make each other ambiguous. |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/README.md:61:| `projection.ts` | Projects scorer internals into caller-facing output. Its `COMMAND_BRIDGES` list is the generated block that `derive-command-bridges.cjs` writes, with an `ownerSkill` on each row. |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/README.md:74:| Aliases | Keep command/skill aliases fixed and explicit. Do not use fuzzy or prefix matching. |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/README.md:82:  -> alias-aware route comparison when scenario expectations use command ids\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/README.md:94:| `aliases.ts` | TypeScript module | Canonical command/skill alias helpers. |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/scorer/README.md:46:| `same-owner-ambiguity.vitest.ts` | Checks that a command row and the skill that owns it never read as ambiguous, while two unrelated skills or a command next to a non-owner still do. |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/scorer/README.md:48:The meaning anchor for command rows in `fusion.ts` is tested one level up, in `../command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts`.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md:3:description: \"Doctor routes from the doctor route manifest become advisor command bridges, so setup and health prompts surface a runnable /doctor:x line.\"\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md:5:  - \"doctor command routing\"\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md:6:  - \"doctor command bridges\"\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md:7:  - \"runnable doctor command line\"\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md:17:Doctor routes from the doctor route manifest become advisor command bridges, so setup and health prompts surface a runnable /doctor:x line.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md:19:A passing skill keeps first place on a contested prompt and the doctor command shows as a second line. A doctor phrase listed in its route's `lead_phrases` is the exception: it ranks the doctor command first, which is how `check my environment variables` keeps `/doctor:env` ahead of system-spec-kit. The Python fallback matches a doctor bridge only on a typed slash command.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md:27:`derive-command-bridges.cjs` reads `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml` as a third inventory source. Each route becomes one bridge `command-doctor-<command>-<target>`, or `command-doctor-<command>` when the command owns one route. Each standalone command becomes one bridge. Each `mcp_subroutes` entry becomes one bridge `command-doctor-mcp-<sub_action>`. The owning skill comes from the router's `skill_agent` tag. Each route needs a hand-written entry in both the `typescript` and `python` lists in `scoring-compatibility.json`. The deriver fills the TypeScript keywords from the manifest's trigger phrases and the Python slash markers from the runnable string, plus the bare command for a route that declares `default_target`. Every derived doctor bridge is active, `command-doctor-helper`, the three `command-doctor-agents-md-*` bridges, the three `command-doctor-symlink-*` bridges and `command-doctor-install` included, so the activation list names a bridge once and the reach probe proves every phrase it carries; a route added without its entry stays derived and unrouted until that entry lands. A route whose manifest class is `read-only` also gets `readOnly: true` in its generated bridge.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md:31:A doctor bridge passes on its own wording, an explicit-author match on one of its manifest phrases or its runnable string. With the local embedder running it can also pass on meaning, as [command-meaning-matching.md](./command-meaning-matching.md) describes. When none passes and none was typed, the scorer asks `/doctor:helper`'s ranker whether the prompt describes a doctor problem, and if it does the command the ranker puts first passes by name when its policy is `run`, and `/doctor:helper` passes instead when that command asks first or has no bridge. A prompt that asks for a `repair path` or says `I have a problem`, with no ranked command and no passing skill, gets `/doctor:helper`. `stopped converging` counts as a wrong state beside a passing skill. Beside a passing skill this needs a wrong state or health check in the prompt, so ordinary requests that share doctor words get no doctor line. A `/doctor:` command counts as typed when the prompt starts with `/doctor:` or when it directly follows `run`, `execute`, `start`, `launch`, `use` or `kick off` outside quotes and backticks. A quoted command or a bare mid-sentence mention does not count. A typed command puts its own passing bridge first. For other prompts, a passing skill stays first and passing doctor bridges sit right after the second passing skill or the only passing skill. This keeps a doctor line within the CLI's three shown results. Doctor bridges never change skill scores. The scorer computes skill ambiguity and abstention as if no doctor bridge existed. The Python native wrapper keeps the same order. A read-only question, such as a list or show prompt, holds every candidate under the read-only confidence floor, unless the prompt names the skill, a command bridge marked `readOnly` matches one of its own phrases, or a skill-specific rule lifts it. A prompt with a no-write phrase, such as `no edits` or `just list`, gets none of these lifts. Mutating bridges stay gated.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md:35:The renderer reads a generated lookup of runnable strings, so a doctor bridge shows as `/doctor:git setup` and never as its raw id. An unmapped doctor id renders nothing. When a doctor bridge is the top pick it is the top line. When a skill is first and a doctor bridge also passes, the brief adds `Also: /doctor:<command> <target>` inside the same token cap. For no-match and outage prompts, the fallback adds one sentence naming `/doctor:setup` when the setup check matches. The check matches set up, set-up or setup wording, install or reinstall wording including installation and installer, configure or configuration wording or `check` followed within three words by environment, env, config, hooks, tools, tooling, toolchain or skilled. The command also checks the advisor. The Claude hook sets the flag, Pi passes it on the deadline fallback and the OpenCode plugin uses its copy of the setup check. The renderer never reads prompt text.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md:39:`doctor-phrase-reach.cjs` keeps the three results shown by the CLI in the reach check. Its rank-first check requires the runnable doctor command, and it rejects any activated phrase with fewer than three words. `/doctor:skill-advisor router-reach` runs it.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md:49:| `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml` | Script | Doctor route manifest and trigger phrases |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md:50:| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs` | Script | Third inventory source, runtime fields and the renderer lookup block |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md:51:| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/scoring-compatibility.json` | Script | Activation of each admitted doctor bridge |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md:58:| `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/doctor-phrase-reach.cjs` | Script | Doctor reach probe |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md:65:| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/doctor-command-bridges.vitest.ts` | Vitest | Manifest-to-bridge parity |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md:69:| `Playbook scenarios [DOC-385](../../../../manual-testing-playbook/doctor-commands/doctor-routing-setup-onboarding.md) to [DOC-391](../../../../manual-testing-playbook/doctor-commands/doctor-setup-run.md).` | Manual playbook | Agent-runnable end-to-end checks |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md:77:- Feature file path: `scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md`\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/README.md:16:`lib/scorer/` contains the native scoring modules used by the skill advisor to rank candidate skills. It combines lane-specific evidence, text matching, age policy, ambiguity handling, explicit alias canonicalization, fusion and output projection into prompt-safe recommendation scores.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/README.md:22:- Canonicalizes narrow command/skill alias groups before campaign scoring compares expected and actual routes.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/README.md:32:+-- age-policy.ts            # Age-aware ranking policy\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/README.md:33:+-- aliases.ts               # Narrow command/skill alias canonicalization\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/README.md:55:| `fusion.ts` | Combines lane scores into final advisor ranking signals through RRF fusion, with a conflict-match rerank seam and a self-recommendation guard that penalizes advisor self-recommendations. `requireCommandPhraseAnchor` keeps a passing command row passing only when the explicit-author lane matched one of its own phrases or its slash string, or when it passes on meaning: a real embedder cosine of at least `COMMAND_MEANING_MIN_COSINE` (0.72) with a lead of `COMMAND_MEANING_MARGIN` (0.02) over the next command row. The word-overlap stand-in used under test never counts. `commandMeaningEligible` decides who may pass on meaning: a prompt matching `NO_EDIT_REQUEST`, the pattern `readOnlyRouteAllowed` also reads, rules out every command, and a read-only explainer admits only a command whose route only reads. `rankMeaningPassedCommandFirst` moves a meaning-passed command ahead of the top passing skill only when its cosine leads that skill's by the same margin. |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/README.md:57:| `aliases.ts` | Canonicalizes explicit command/skill alias groups for route comparisons. |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/README.md:59:| `ambiguity.ts` | Detects close or unclear recommendation states. A command row and its `ownerSkill` count as one answer, so they never make each other ambiguous. |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/README.md:61:| `projection.ts` | Projects scorer internals into caller-facing output. Its `COMMAND_BRIDGES` list is the generated block that `derive-command-bridges.cjs` writes, with an `ownerSkill` on each row. |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/README.md:74:| Aliases | Keep command/skill aliases fixed and explicit. Do not use fuzzy or prefix matching. |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/README.md:82:  -> alias-aware route comparison when scenario expectations use command ids\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/README.md:94:| `aliases.ts` | TypeScript module | Canonical command/skill alias helpers. |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/scorer/README.md:46:| `same-owner-ambiguity.vitest.ts` | Checks that a command row and the skill that owns it never read as ambiguous, while two unrelated skills or a command next to a non-owner still do. |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/scorer/README.md:48:The meaning anchor for command rows in `fusion.ts` is tested one level up, in `../command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts`.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md:3:description: \"Doctor routes from the doctor route manifest become advisor command bridges, so setup and health prompts surface a runnable /doctor:x line.\"\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md:5:  - \"doctor command routing\"\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md:6:  - \"doctor command bridges\"\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md:7:  - \"runnable doctor command line\"\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md:17:Doctor routes from the doctor route manifest become advisor command bridges, so setup and health prompts surface a runnable /doctor:x line.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md:19:A passing skill keeps first place on a contested prompt and the doctor command shows as a second line. A doctor phrase listed in its route's `lead_phrases` is the exception: it ranks the doctor command first, which is how `check my environment variables` keeps `/doctor:env` ahead of system-spec-kit. The Python fallback matches a doctor bridge only on a typed slash command.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md:27:`derive-command-bridges.cjs` reads `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml` as a third inventory source. Each route becomes one bridge `command-doctor-<command>-<target>`, or `command-doctor-<command>` when the command owns one route. Each standalone command becomes one bridge. Each `mcp_subroutes` entry becomes one bridge `command-doctor-mcp-<sub_action>`. The owning skill comes from the router's `skill_agent` tag. Each route needs a hand-written entry in both the `typescript` and `python` lists in `scoring-compatibility.json`. The deriver fills the TypeScript keywords from the manifest's trigger phrases and the Python slash markers from the runnable string, plus the bare command for a route that declares `default_target`. Every derived doctor bridge is active, `command-doctor-helper`, the three `command-doctor-agents-md-*` bridges, the three `command-doctor-symlink-*` bridges and `command-doctor-install` included, so the activation list names a bridge once and the reach probe proves every phrase it carries; a route added without its entry stays derived and unrouted until that entry lands. A route whose manifest class is `read-only` also gets `readOnly: true` in its generated bridge.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md:31:A doctor bridge passes on its own wording, an explicit-author match on one of its manifest phrases or its runnable string. With the local embedder running it can also pass on meaning, as [command-meaning-matching.md](./command-meaning-matching.md) describes. When none passes and none was typed, the scorer asks `/doctor:helper`'s ranker whether the prompt describes a doctor problem, and if it does the command the ranker puts first passes by name when its policy is `run`, and `/doctor:helper` passes instead when that command asks first or has no bridge. A prompt that asks for a `repair path` or says `I have a problem`, with no ranked command and no passing skill, gets `/doctor:helper`. `stopped converging` counts as a wrong state beside a passing skill. Beside a passing skill this needs a wrong state or health check in the prompt, so ordinary requests that share doctor words get no doctor line. A `/doctor:` command counts as typed when the prompt starts with `/doctor:` or when it directly follows `run`, `execute`, `start`, `launch`, `use` or `kick off` outside quotes and backticks. A quoted command or a bare mid-sentence mention does not count. A typed command puts its own passing bridge first. For other prompts, a passing skill stays first and passing doctor bridges sit right after the second passing skill or the only passing skill. This keeps a doctor line within the CLI's three shown results. Doctor bridges never change skill scores. The scorer computes skill ambiguity and abstention as if no doctor bridge existed. The Python native wrapper keeps the same order. A read-only question, such as a list or show prompt, holds every candidate under the read-only confidence floor, unless the prompt names the skill, a command bridge marked `readOnly` matches one of its own phrases, or a skill-specific rule lifts it. A prompt with a no-write phrase, such as `no edits` or `just list`, gets none of these lifts. Mutating bridges stay gated.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md:35:The renderer reads a generated lookup of runnable strings, so a doctor bridge shows as `/doctor:git setup` and never as its raw id. An unmapped doctor id renders nothing. When a doctor bridge is the top pick it is the top line. When a skill is first and a doctor bridge also passes, the brief adds `Also: /doctor:<command> <target>` inside the same token cap. For no-match and outage prompts, the fallback adds one sentence naming `/doctor:setup` when the setup check matches. The check matches set up, set-up or setup wording, install or reinstall wording including installation and installer, configure or configuration wording or `check` followed within three words by environment, env, config, hooks, tools, tooling, toolchain or skilled. The command also checks the advisor. The Claude hook sets the flag, Pi passes it on the deadline fallback and the OpenCode plugin uses its copy of the setup check. The renderer never reads prompt text.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md:39:`doctor-phrase-reach.cjs` keeps the three results shown by the CLI in the reach check. Its rank-first check requires the runnable doctor command, and it rejects any activated phrase with fewer than three words. `/doctor:skill-advisor router-reach` runs it.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md:49:| `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml` | Script | Doctor route manifest and trigger phrases |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md:50:| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs` | Script | Third inventory source, runtime fields and the renderer lookup block |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md:51:| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/scoring-compatibility.json` | Script | Activation of each admitted doctor bridge |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md:58:| `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/doctor-phrase-reach.cjs` | Script | Doctor reach probe |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md:65:| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/doctor-command-bridges.vitest.ts` | Vitest | Manifest-to-bridge parity |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md:69:| `Playbook scenarios [DOC-385](../../../../manual-testing-playbook/doctor-commands/doctor-routing-setup-onboarding.md) to [DOC-391](../../../../manual-testing-playbook/doctor-commands/doctor-setup-run.md).` | Manual playbook | Agent-runnable end-to-end checks |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md:77:- Feature file path: `scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md`\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research; grep -n \\\"command\\\\|45\\\\|46\\\\|attach\\\\|policy\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/README.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/scorer/README.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md | head -50\"}"},"time":{"start":1794550919172,"end":1794550919841}}}}
