{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794551104672,"sessionID":"ses_e2c7999e1ffeYcD6BDSYeMhQPJ","part":{"partID":"prt_1d394c02100273P5rdBVQL1fDY","sessionID":"ses_e2c7999e1ffeYcD6BDSYeMhQPJ","messageID":"msg_1d394852a00140k7VqoIfRx4oS","type":"tool","id":"call_309cb17b1fb54b5cae047ae1","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research; git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff -U0 35c3188681..320e7b64d4 -- .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ARCHITECTURE.md | grep -E \"^[+-].*(45|46|Cursor|dsh|command rows)\" | head -20"},"output":"-The advisor ships prompt-submit adapters for Claude, Codex, Cursor, Devin and Pi, plus the OpenCode plugin at `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js`. The native adapters and Pi run the same hook handler, which gates the prompt, calls the advisor CLI and renders with `renderAdvisorBrief`; the OpenCode plugin calls the CLI itself. When the handler has no brief, including after a timeout or a no-route result, it emits the directives fallback and lets the prompt proceed. The Claude adapter applies `SPECKIT_CLAUDE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS` to its advisor subprocess. When the operator leaves it unset, the Claude shim sets 2,200 ms for the hook under its own 2,500 ms kill so the fallback prints in time. Pi runs the handler in-process and races it against the budget plus 300 ms. The hook's request skips compiled-route enrichment with `includeCompiledRoute: false`. The OpenCode plugin does not send that option. The plugin appends the brief to the system prompt and exposes the advisor status tool.\n+The advisor ships prompt-submit adapters for Claude, Codex, Cursor, Devin and Pi, plus the OpenCode plugin at `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js`. The native adapters and Pi run the same hook handler, which gates the prompt, calls the advisor CLI and renders with `renderAdvisorBrief`; the OpenCode plugin calls the CLI itself. When the handler has no brief, including after a timeout or a no-route result, it emits the directives fallback and lets the prompt proceed. The Claude adapter applies `SPECKIT_CLAUDE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS` to its advisor subprocess. When the operator leaves it unset, the Claude shim sets 2,200 ms for the hook under its own 2,500 ms kill so the fallback prints in time. Pi runs the handler in-process and races it against the budget plus 300 ms. The hook's request sends `includeCompiledRoute: true`, because the advisor derives a recommendation's slash command from the compiled route. The hook keeps that `command` field and reads nothing from the route itself. The OpenCode plugin does not send the option and gets the default of true. The plugin appends the brief to the system prompt and exposes the advisor status tool.\n+Command rows use the same embedder. The bridge deriver writes an `embeddingText` for each of the 45 command rows the TypeScript scorer serves, and `skill_graph_scan` embeds it into its own `vec_cmd_<dim>` table beside the skill vectors. The scan skips a row whose text has not changed and prunes a row that is no longer generated. A command row normally passes only on one of its own phrases or its slash string. It can also pass on meaning: the prompt's real embedding has to reach a cosine of 0.72 against the row and lead the next command row by 0.02. A command that passed this way ranks first only when it leads the top passing skill by the same 0.02. A prompt that asks for no change, such as \"no edits\" or \"just list\", rules out every command on meaning. A read-only question lets only a command whose route only reads pass on meaning. Without the local embedder (Ollama serving `nomic-embed-text`) no cosine exists, so command rows pass on their phrases alone.\n+`derive-command-bridges.cjs` writes an `embeddingText` for each command row the TypeScript scorer serves, 45 rows in all. A metadata row leads with its `userIntent.job` sentence and adds its owned phrases. The `description` stands in only when the record states no job. A doctor row uses its router's frontmatter `description` and the route's trigger phrases. Slash command strings are stripped from the text.\n+- [doctor-command-routing.md](./doctor-command-routing.md) - The phrase anchor that command rows pass on by default.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"-The advisor ships prompt-submit adapters for Claude, Codex, Cursor, Devin and Pi, plus the OpenCode plugin at `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js`. The native adapters and Pi run the same hook handler, which gates the prompt, calls the advisor CLI and renders with `renderAdvisorBrief`; the OpenCode plugin calls the CLI itself. When the handler has no brief, including after a timeout or a no-route result, it emits the directives fallback and lets the prompt proceed. The Claude adapter applies `SPECKIT_CLAUDE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS` to its advisor subprocess. When the operator leaves it unset, the Claude shim sets 2,200 ms for the hook under its own 2,500 ms kill so the fallback prints in time. Pi runs the handler in-process and races it against the budget plus 300 ms. The hook's request skips compiled-route enrichment with `includeCompiledRoute: false`. The OpenCode plugin does not send that option. The plugin appends the brief to the system prompt and exposes the advisor status tool.\n+The advisor ships prompt-submit adapters for Claude, Codex, Cursor, Devin and Pi, plus the OpenCode plugin at `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js`. The native adapters and Pi run the same hook handler, which gates the prompt, calls the advisor CLI and renders with `renderAdvisorBrief`; the OpenCode plugin calls the CLI itself. When the handler has no brief, including after a timeout or a no-route result, it emits the directives fallback and lets the prompt proceed. The Claude adapter applies `SPECKIT_CLAUDE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS` to its advisor subprocess. When the operator leaves it unset, the Claude shim sets 2,200 ms for the hook under its own 2,500 ms kill so the fallback prints in time. Pi runs the handler in-process and races it against the budget plus 300 ms. The hook's request sends `includeCompiledRoute: true`, because the advisor derives a recommendation's slash command from the compiled route. The hook keeps that `command` field and reads nothing from the route itself. The OpenCode plugin does not send the option and gets the default of true. The plugin appends the brief to the system prompt and exposes the advisor status tool.\n+Command rows use the same embedder. The bridge deriver writes an `embeddingText` for each of the 45 command rows the TypeScript scorer serves, and `skill_graph_scan` embeds it into its own `vec_cmd_<dim>` table beside the skill vectors. The scan skips a row whose text has not changed and prunes a row that is no longer generated. A command row normally passes only on one of its own phrases or its slash string. It can also pass on meaning: the prompt's real embedding has to reach a cosine of 0.72 against the row and lead the next command row by 0.02. A command that passed this way ranks first only when it leads the top passing skill by the same 0.02. A prompt that asks for no change, such as \"no edits\" or \"just list\", rules out every command on meaning. A read-only question lets only a command whose route only reads pass on meaning. Without the local embedder (Ollama serving `nomic-embed-text`) no cosine exists, so command rows pass on their phrases alone.\n+`derive-command-bridges.cjs` writes an `embeddingText` for each command row the TypeScript scorer serves, 45 rows in all. A metadata row leads with its `userIntent.job` sentence and adds its owned phrases. The `description` stands in only when the record states no job. A doctor row uses its router's frontmatter `description` and the route's trigger phrases. Slash command strings are stripped from the text.\n+- [doctor-command-routing.md](./doctor-command-routing.md) - The phrase anchor that command rows pass on by default.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research; git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff -U0 35c3188681..320e7b64d4 -- .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ARCHITECTURE.md | grep -E \\\"^[+-].*(45|46|Cursor|dsh|command rows)\\\" | head -20\"}"},"time":{"start":1794551103521,"end":1794551104672}}}}
