{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794551290085,"sessionID":"ses_e2c7999e1ffeYcD6BDSYeMhQPJ","part":{"partID":"prt_1d3974c7e001V1hRzqzcCujz2z","sessionID":"ses_e2c7999e1ffeYcD6BDSYeMhQPJ","messageID":"msg_1d3973ba1001rE3CFVnve7ax8j","type":"tool","id":"call_dd9219e7404b4c3bb40a250d","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach/deep-review-strategy.md","content":"---\ntitle: Deep Review Strategy - scorer-attach lineage\ndescription: Runtime strategy tracking review progress, dimension coverage, findings, and outcomes across iterations for the scorer-attach fan-out lineage.\nversion: 1.11.14.0\n---\n\n# Deep Review Strategy - scorer-attach lineage\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Purpose\n\nPersistent brain for this fan-out lineage. It records which dimensions remain, what was found\n(P0/P1/P2), which review approaches worked or failed, and where to focus next. Read at every\niteration before any review action.\n\n### Ownership\n\nMachine-managed metrics and coverage blocks are wrapped in explicit ownership markers. Human\ncommentary and operator overrides live outside those markers.\n\n---\n\n## 2. TOPIC\n\nReview: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (scorer-attach).\nScope: the 67 `scorer-attach` paths in `review/review-scope.txt` plus the 29 `shared` docs that\ndescribe them — the advisor's command-surfacing surface: `lib/command-attach.ts`, the generated\ncommand tables, `derive-command-bridges.cjs`, the recommend/status handlers, the scorer modules\nthat gate command rows (`fusion.ts`, `ambiguity.ts`, `doctor-helper-handoff.ts`, `projection.ts`),\nthe schemas, the generated projection JSON, and their tests and docs.\n\n---\n\n## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n- [ ] D1 Correctness, Logic errors, off-by-one, wrong return types, broken invariants\n- [ ] D2 Security, Injection, auth bypass, secrets exposure, unsafe deserialization\n- [ ] D3 Traceability, Spec/code alignment, checklist evidence, cross-reference integrity\n- [ ] D4 Maintainability, Patterns, clarity, documentation quality, safe follow-on change cost\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n\n- The doctor command implementations and route manifest content (`doctor-install` lineage owns them);\n  this lineage reads them only as context evidence for the derived policy table.\n- The hook renderers and session readers (`render-hooks-plugin` lineage owns them); this lineage reads\n  `lib/render.ts` only to confirm how a surfaced `policy` reaches a reader.\n- The accuracy runner, holdout builder and command transcript scorer (`accuracy-runner` lineage owns\n  them); holdout hygiene here means proving this lineage's surface never reads or prints holdout rows.\n- The compiled-routing engine internals (`.skilled/bin/lib/compiled-routing/**`); this lineage treats a\n  route decision as an input contract.\n- No code changes: review is observation-only.\n\n---\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n\n- Convergence: `newFindingsRatio` at or below `convergenceThreshold` 0.10 with no active P0/P1.\n- Cap: `maxIterations` 5.\n- Stuck: two consecutive iterations with no new evidence (stuckThreshold 2).\n- Any active P0 blocks PASS regardless of convergence.\n\n---\n\n## 6. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n[None yet -- populated as iterations complete dimension reviews]\n\n| Dimension | Verdict | Iteration | Summary |\n|-----------|---------|-----------|---------|\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 7. RUNNING FINDINGS\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n- **P0 (Critical):** 0 active\n- **P1 (Major):** 0 active\n- **P2 (Minor):** 0 active\n- **Delta this iteration:** +0 P0, +0 P1, +0 P2\n\n[Findings are tracked in `deep-review-findings-registry.json`. This section provides a running count summary updated after each iteration.]\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n\n---\n\n## 10. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n\n[Populated when a review approach has been tried from multiple angles without yielding new findings]\n\n---\n\n## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n- Completed pivots: 0\n- Failed pivots: 0\n- Audited overrides: 0\n- Swept: none yet\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n\n[Review angles that were investigated and definitively eliminated -- consolidated from iteration dead-end data]\n\n---\n\n## 12. NEXT FOCUS\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n- Dimension: correctness\n- Focus area: `attachCommand` / `typedCommandForTop` / `commandRowFor` semantics in `lib/command-attach.ts`, and their consumers in `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` and `lib/scorer/fusion.ts`\n- Reason: iteration 1 opens the loop on the command-attach surface, which is the changed code the lineage label names\n- Rotation status: new dimension\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: none yet\n- Required evidence: `file:line` for every finding plus a unit-level reproduction of the failing input\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\n\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\n\n- Target pointers: `lib/command-attach.ts` (generated `MODE_COMMANDS`, `COMMAND_ROWS`,\n  `COMMAND_POLICIES`, `TRACKED_COMMANDS`; `attachCommand`, `typedCommandForTop`, `routeNeedsMode`),\n  `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` (`enrichCompiledRoutes`, `attachTypedCommand`, `publicRecommendation`),\n  `lib/scorer/fusion.ts` (`requireCommandPhraseAnchor`, `commandMeaningEligible`, `readOnlyRouteAllowed`,\n  `applyDoctorHelperHandoff`, `rankTypedCommandOwnerFirst`), `lib/scorer/ambiguity.ts`,\n  `lib/scorer/doctor-helper-handoff.ts`, `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts`,\n  `runtime/scripts/command-bridges/*`, `feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/*.md`,\n  shared `README.md` / `ARCHITECTURE.md` for the advisor.\n- Behavior claims: a single-mode compiled route attaches the hub's slash command; a typed command\n  travels through its owner only; policy is `run` only for a read-only or spec-folder-confined\n  add-only command; a mutating command is never offered with `run`; a meaning-passed command row\n  needs a real cosine of 0.72 and a 0.02 lead; a no-edit prompt rules out every command.\n- Reuse and conventions: generated blocks are deriver output, never hand-edited; generated data is\n  drift-guarded by `command-bridges-drift-guard.vitest.ts`; `review-core.md` severity/evidence rules.\n- Review risks and gaps: `resource-map.md` absent (coverage gate skipped); holdout-bearing scripts\n  live outside this lineage; the router's mode selection is an upstream input that was not executed\n  (no write-safe way to probe it), so route-dependent findings state the reach condition.\n- Out of scope: doctor implementations, hook renderers, accuracy runner, compiled-routing engine.\n\n---\n\n## 14. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n[Alignment checks completed across core and overlay protocols]\n\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\n|----------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|\n| `spec_code` | core | pending | - | - |\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | pending | - | - |\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | notApplicable | - | no playbook path in this surface |\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 15. FILES UNDER REVIEW\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n[Per-file coverage state table -- populated during initialization from scope discovery]\n\n| File | Dimensions Reviewed | Last Iteration | Findings | Status |\n|------|-------------------|----------------|----------|--------|\n| (see `deep-review-config.json` `reviewScopeFiles`, 96 paths) | - | - | - | pending |\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 16. REVIEW BOUNDARIES\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n- Max iterations: 5\n- Convergence threshold: 0.1\n- Rolling STOP threshold: 0.08\n- No-progress threshold: 0.05\n- Coverage stabilization passes required: 1\n- Session lineage: sessionId=fanout-scorer-attach-1794550137809-1ecgc7, parentSessionId=null, generation=1, lineageMode=new\n- Findings registry: `deep-review-findings-registry.json`\n- Release-readiness states: in-progress | converged | release-blocking\n- Per-iteration budget: 13 tool calls, 10 minutes\n- Severity threshold: P2\n- Review target type: spec-folder\n- Cross-reference checks: core=[spec_code, checklist_evidence], overlay=[skill_agent, agent_cross_runtime, feature_catalog_code, playbook_capability]\n- Started: 2026-11-13T06:27:27Z\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach/deep-review-strategy.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach/deep-review-strategy.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach/deep-review-strategy.md\",\"content\":\"---\\ntitle: Deep Review Strategy - scorer-attach lineage\\ndescription: Runtime strategy tracking review progress, dimension coverage, findings, and outcomes across iterations for the scorer-attach fan-out lineage.\\nversion: 1.11.14.0\\n---\\n\\n# Deep Review Strategy - scorer-attach lineage\\n\\n## 1. OVERVIEW\\n\\n### Purpose\\n\\nPersistent brain for this fan-out lineage. It records which dimensions remain, what was found\\n(P0/P1/P2), which review approaches worked or failed, and where to focus next. Read at every\\niteration before any review action.\\n\\n### Ownership\\n\\nMachine-managed metrics and coverage blocks are wrapped in explicit ownership markers. Human\\ncommentary and operator overrides live outside those markers.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. TOPIC\\n\\nReview: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (scorer-attach).\\nScope: the 67 `scorer-attach` paths in `review/review-scope.txt` plus the 29 `shared` docs that\\ndescribe them — the advisor's command-surfacing surface: `lib/command-attach.ts`, the generated\\ncommand tables, `derive-command-bridges.cjs`, the recommend/status handlers, the scorer modules\\nthat gate command rows (`fusion.ts`, `ambiguity.ts`, `doctor-helper-handoff.ts`, `projection.ts`),\\nthe schemas, the generated projection JSON, and their tests and docs.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\n- [ ] D1 Correctness, Logic errors, off-by-one, wrong return types, broken invariants\\n- [ ] D2 Security, Injection, auth bypass, secrets exposure, unsafe deserialization\\n- [ ] D3 Traceability, Spec/code alignment, checklist evidence, cross-reference integrity\\n- [ ] D4 Maintainability, Patterns, clarity, documentation quality, safe follow-on change cost\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. NON-GOALS\\n\\n- The doctor command implementations and route manifest content (`doctor-install` lineage owns them);\\n  this lineage reads them only as context evidence for the derived policy table.\\n- The hook renderers and session readers (`render-hooks-plugin` lineage owns them); this lineage reads\\n  `lib/render.ts` only to confirm how a surfaced `policy` reaches a reader.\\n- The accuracy runner, holdout builder and command transcript scorer (`accuracy-runner` lineage owns\\n  them); holdout hygiene here means proving this lineage's surface never reads or prints holdout rows.\\n- The compiled-routing engine internals (`.skilled/bin/lib/compiled-routing/**`); this lineage treats a\\n  route decision as an input contract.\\n- No code changes: review is observation-only.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\\n\\n- Convergence: `newFindingsRatio` at or below `convergenceThreshold` 0.10 with no active P0/P1.\\n- Cap: `maxIterations` 5.\\n- Stuck: two consecutive iterations with no new evidence (stuckThreshold 2).\\n- Any active P0 blocks PASS regardless of convergence.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\n[None yet -- populated as iterations complete dimension reviews]\\n\\n| Dimension | Verdict | Iteration | Summary |\\n|-----------|---------|-----------|---------|\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. RUNNING FINDINGS\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\n- **P0 (Critical):** 0 active\\n- **P1 (Major):** 0 active\\n- **P2 (Minor):** 0 active\\n- **Delta this iteration:** +0 P0, +0 P1, +0 P2\\n\\n[Findings are tracked in `deep-review-findings-registry.json`. This section provides a running count summary updated after each iteration.]\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\\n\\n[Populated when a review approach has been tried from multiple angles without yielding new findings]\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\n- Completed pivots: 0\\n- Failed pivots: 0\\n- Audited overrides: 0\\n- Swept: none yet\\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\\n\\n[Review angles that were investigated and definitively eliminated -- consolidated from iteration dead-end data]\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 12. NEXT FOCUS\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\n- Dimension: correctness\\n- Focus area: `attachCommand` / `typedCommandForTop` / `commandRowFor` semantics in `lib/command-attach.ts`, and their consumers in `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` and `lib/scorer/fusion.ts`\\n- Reason: iteration 1 opens the loop on the command-attach surface, which is the changed code the lineage label names\\n- Rotation status: new dimension\\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: none yet\\n- Required evidence: `file:line` for every finding plus a unit-level reproduction of the failing input\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\\n\\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\\n\\n- Target pointers: `lib/command-attach.ts` (generated `MODE_COMMANDS`, `COMMAND_ROWS`,\\n  `COMMAND_POLICIES`, `TRACKED_COMMANDS`; `attachCommand`, `typedCommandForTop`, `routeNeedsMode`),\\n  `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` (`enrichCompiledRoutes`, `attachTypedCommand`, `publicRecommendation`),\\n  `lib/scorer/fusion.ts` (`requireCommandPhraseAnchor`, `commandMeaningEligible`, `readOnlyRouteAllowed`,\\n  `applyDoctorHelperHandoff`, `rankTypedCommandOwnerFirst`), `lib/scorer/ambiguity.ts`,\\n  `lib/scorer/doctor-helper-handoff.ts`, `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts`,\\n  `runtime/scripts/command-bridges/*`, `feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/*.md`,\\n  shared `README.md` / `ARCHITECTURE.md` for the advisor.\\n- Behavior claims: a single-mode compiled route attaches the hub's slash command; a typed command\\n  travels through its owner only; policy is `run` only for a read-only or spec-folder-confined\\n  add-only command; a mutating command is never offered with `run`; a meaning-passed command row\\n  needs a real cosine of 0.72 and a 0.02 lead; a no-edit prompt rules out every command.\\n- Reuse and conventions: generated blocks are deriver output, never hand-edited; generated data is\\n  drift-guarded by `command-bridges-drift-guard.vitest.ts`; `review-core.md` severity/evidence rules.\\n- Review risks and gaps: `resource-map.md` absent (coverage gate skipped); holdout-bearing scripts\\n  live outside this lineage; the router's mode selection is an upstream input that was not executed\\n  (no write-safe way to probe it), so route-dependent findings state the reach condition.\\n- Out of scope: doctor implementations, hook renderers, accuracy runner, compiled-routing engine.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 14. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\n[Alignment checks completed across core and overlay protocols]\\n\\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\\n|----------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|\\n| `spec_code` | core | pending | - | - |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | pending | - | - |\\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | pending | - | - |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | pending | - | - |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pending | - | - |\\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | notApplicable | - | no playbook path in this surface |\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 15. FILES UNDER REVIEW\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\n[Per-file coverage state table -- populated during initialization from scope discovery]\\n\\n| File | Dimensions Reviewed | Last Iteration | Findings | Status |\\n|------|-------------------|----------------|----------|--------|\\n| (see `deep-review-config.json` `reviewScopeFiles`, 96 paths) | - | - | - | pending |\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 16. REVIEW BOUNDARIES\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\n- Max iterations: 5\\n- Convergence threshold: 0.1\\n- Rolling STOP threshold: 0.08\\n- No-progress threshold: 0.05\\n- Coverage stabilization passes required: 1\\n- Session lineage: sessionId=fanout-scorer-attach-1794550137809-1ecgc7, parentSessionId=null, generation=1, lineageMode=new\\n- Findings registry: `deep-review-findings-registry.json`\\n- Release-readiness states: in-progress | converged | release-blocking\\n- Per-iteration budget: 13 tool calls, 10 minutes\\n- Severity threshold: P2\