{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794551371756,"sessionID":"ses_e2c7999e1ffeYcD6BDSYeMhQPJ","part":{"partID":"prt_1d398d6b2001xfOiM7t4CTpX0o","sessionID":"ses_e2c7999e1ffeYcD6BDSYeMhQPJ","messageID":"msg_1d398c573001UuSoqga4EpLHsj","type":"tool","id":"call_048af37df8de4892816942f4","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach/deep-review-strategy.md, lines 1-182\n1: ---\n2: title: Deep Review Strategy - scorer-attach lineage\n3: description: Runtime strategy tracking review progress, dimension coverage, findings, and outcomes across iterations for the scorer-attach fan-out lineage.\n4: version: 1.11.14.0\n5: ---\n6: \n7: # Deep Review Strategy - scorer-attach lineage\n8: \n9: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n10: \n11: ### Purpose\n12: \n13: Persistent brain for this fan-out lineage. It records which dimensions remain, what was found\n14: (P0/P1/P2), which review approaches worked or failed, and where to focus next. Read at every\n15: iteration before any review action.\n16: \n17: ### Ownership\n18: \n19: Machine-managed metrics and coverage blocks are wrapped in explicit ownership markers. Human\n20: commentary and operator overrides live outside those markers.\n21: \n22: ---\n23: \n24: ## 2. TOPIC\n25: \n26: Review: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (scorer-attach).\n27: Scope: the 67 `scorer-attach` paths in `review/review-scope.txt` plus the 29 `shared` docs that\n28: describe them — the advisor's command-surfacing surface: `lib/command-attach.ts`, the generated\n29: command tables, `derive-command-bridges.cjs`, the recommend/status handlers, the scorer modules\n30: that gate command rows (`fusion.ts`, `ambiguity.ts`, `doctor-helper-handoff.ts`, `projection.ts`),\n31: the schemas, the generated projection JSON, and their tests and docs.\n32: \n33: ---\n34: \n35: <!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n36: ## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n37: - [ ] correctness\n38: - [ ] security\n39: - [ ] traceability\n40: - [ ] maintainability\n41: \n42: <!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n43: ## 4. NON-GOALS\n44: \n45: - The doctor command implementations and route manifest content (`doctor-install` lineage owns them);\n46:   this lineage reads them only as context evidence for the derived policy table.\n47: - The hook renderers and session readers (`render-hooks-plugin` lineage owns them); this lineage reads\n48:   `lib/render.ts` only to confirm how a surfaced `policy` reaches a reader.\n49: - The accuracy runner, holdout builder and command transcript scorer (`accuracy-runner` lineage owns\n50:   them); holdout hygiene here means proving this lineage's surface never reads or prints holdout rows.\n51: - The compiled-routing engine internals (`.skilled/bin/lib/compiled-routing/**`); this lineage treats a\n52:   route decision as an input contract.\n53: - No code changes: review is observation-only.\n54: \n55: ---\n56: \n57: ## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n58: \n59: - Convergence: `newFindingsRatio` at or below `convergenceThreshold` 0.10 with no active P0/P1.\n60: - Cap: `maxIterations` 5.\n61: - Stuck: two consecutive iterations with no new evidence (stuckThreshold 2).\n62: - Any active P0 blocks PASS regardless of convergence.\n63: \n64: ---\n65: \n66: <!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n67: ## 4. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n68: [None yet]\n69: \n70: <!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n71: <!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n72: ## 5. RUNNING FINDINGS\n73: - P0 (Blockers): 0\n74: - P1 (Required): 0\n75: - P2 (Suggestions): 0\n76: - Resolved: 0\n77: \n78: <!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n79: ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n80: \n81: [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n82: \n83: ---\n84: \n85: ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n86: \n87: [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n88: \n89: ---\n90: \n91: <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n92: ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n93: [No exhausted approach categories yet]\n94: \n95: <!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n96: ## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\n97: - Completed pivots: 0\n98: - Failed pivots: 0\n99: - Audited overrides: 0\n100: - Swept: none yet\n101: - Pivot lineage: none yet\n102: - Remaining frontier: none recorded\n103: \n104: ## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n105: \n106: [Review angles that were investigated and definitively eliminated -- consolidated from iteration dead-end data]\n107: \n108: ---\n109: \n110: <!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n111: ## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n112: correctness\n113: \n114: <!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n115: ## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\n116: \n117: ### Bounded Context Snapshot\n118: \n119: - Target pointers: `lib/command-attach.ts` (generated `MODE_COMMANDS`, `COMMAND_ROWS`,\n120:   `COMMAND_POLICIES`, `TRACKED_COMMANDS`; `attachCommand`, `typedCommandForTop`, `routeNeedsMode`),\n121:   `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` (`enrichCompiledRoutes`, `attachTypedCommand`, `publicRecommendation`),\n122:   `lib/scorer/fusion.ts` (`requireCommandPhraseAnchor`, `commandMeaningEligible`, `readOnlyRouteAllowed`,\n123:   `applyDoctorHelperHandoff`, `rankTypedCommandOwnerFirst`), `lib/scorer/ambiguity.ts`,\n124:   `lib/scorer/doctor-helper-handoff.ts`, `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts`,\n125:   `runtime/scripts/command-bridges/*`, `feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/*.md`,\n126:   shared `README.md` / `ARCHITECTURE.md` for the advisor.\n127: - Behavior claims: a single-mode compiled route attaches the hub's slash command; a typed command\n128:   travels through its owner only; policy is `run` only for a read-only or spec-folder-confined\n129:   add-only command; a mutating command is never offered with `run`; a meaning-passed command row\n130:   needs a real cosine of 0.72 and a 0.02 lead; a no-edit prompt rules out every command.\n131: - Reuse and conventions: generated blocks are deriver output, never hand-edited; generated data is\n132:   drift-guarded by `command-bridges-drift-guard.vitest.ts`; `review-core.md` severity/evidence rules.\n133: - Review risks and gaps: `resource-map.md` absent (coverage gate skipped); holdout-bearing scripts\n134:   live outside this lineage; the router's mode selection is an upstream input that was not executed\n135:   (no write-safe way to probe it), so route-dependent findings state the reach condition.\n136: - Out of scope: doctor implementations, hook renderers, accuracy runner, compiled-routing engine.\n137: \n138: ---\n139: \n140: ## 14. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\n141: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n142: [Alignment checks completed across core and overlay protocols]\n143: \n144: | Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\n145: |----------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|\n146: | `spec_code` | core | pending | - | - |\n147: | `checklist_evidence` | core | pending | - | - |\n148: | `skill_agent` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n149: | `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n150: | `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n151: | `playbook_capability` | overlay | notApplicable | - | no playbook path in this surface |\n152: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n153: \n154: ---\n155: \n156: ## 15. FILES UNDER REVIEW\n157: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n158: [Per-file coverage state table -- populated during initialization from scope discovery]\n159: \n160: | File | Dimensions Reviewed | Last Iteration | Findings | Status |\n161: |------|-------------------|----------------|----------|--------|\n162: | (see `deep-review-config.json` `reviewScopeFiles`, 96 paths) | - | - | - | pending |\n163: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n164: \n165: ---\n166: \n167: ## 16. REVIEW BOUNDARIES\n168: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n169: - Max iterations: 5\n170: - Convergence threshold: 0.1\n171: - Rolling STOP threshold: 0.08\n172: - No-progress