{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794551388026,"sessionID":"ses_e2c7999e1ffeYcD6BDSYeMhQPJ","part":{"partID":"prt_1d3990f3f001Xn7gB4i9WtqPU7","sessionID":"ses_e2c7999e1ffeYcD6BDSYeMhQPJ","messageID":"msg_1d398dd7a001e0Xg4wLf80ffz3","type":"tool","id":"call_b0c4fa51b3f04b5487eadce6","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach/deep-review-strategy.md","oldString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]","newString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n- Executing the shipped module with `node --experimental-strip-types` turned two boundary questions into executed evidence instead of a reading: the `/deep:` bypass and the `/create:skill.md` match both reproduced exactly (iteration 1).\n- Diffing the generated tables against their authored sources (`mode-registry.json`, `_routes.yaml`, `command-metadata.json`) proved three \"missing row\" hypotheses false before they became findings (iteration 1).\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n- Parsing `command-bridges.generated.json` `commandPolicies` as a runnable-keyed map failed: doctor routes are keyed by bare command (`/doctor:git`) while the derived rows key by runnable (`/doctor:git setup`). Discarded that comparison as a methodology error rather than reporting a false drift (iteration 1)."},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -81,15 +81,16 @@\n \n <!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n \n-[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n+- Executing the shipped module with `node --experimental-strip-types` turned two boundary questions into executed evidence instead of a reading: the `/deep:` bypass and the `/create:skill.md` match both reproduced exactly (iteration 1).\n+- Diffing the generated tables against their authored sources (`mode-registry.json`, `_routes.yaml`, `command-metadata.json`) proved three \"missing row\" hypotheses false before they became findings (iteration 1).\n \n ---\n \n ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n \n-[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n+- Parsing `command-bridges.generated.json` `commandPolicies` as a runnable-keyed map failed: doctor routes are keyed by bare command (`/doctor:git`) while the derived rows key by runnable (`/doctor:git setup`). Discarded that comparison as a methodology error rather than reporting a false drift (iteration 1).\n \n ---\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n","status":"modified","additions":3,"deletions":2}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach/deep-review-strategy.md\",\"oldString\":\"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\",\"newString\":\"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n- Executing the shipped module with `node --experimental-strip-types` turned two boundary questions into executed evidence instead of a reading: the `/deep:` bypass and the `/create:skill.md` match both reproduced exactly (iteration 1).\\n- Diffing the generated tables against their authored sources (`mode-registry.json`, `_routes.yaml`, `command-metadata.json`) proved three \\\"missing row\\\" hypotheses false before they became findings (iteration 1).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n- Parsing `command-bridges.generated.json` `commandPolicies` as a runnable-keyed map failed: doctor routes are keyed by bare command (`/doctor:git`) while the derived rows key by runnable (`/doctor:git setup`). Discarded that comparison as a methodology error rather than reporting a false drift (iteration 1).\"}"},"time":{"start":1794551385919,"end":1794551388026}}}}
