{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794551513099,"sessionID":"ses_e2c7999e1ffeYcD6BDSYeMhQPJ","part":{"partID":"prt_1d39a998d001MXQ7J5PoMXzZnv","sessionID":"ses_e2c7999e1ffeYcD6BDSYeMhQPJ","messageID":"msg_1d39a6542001hXiXCfsDYyc6bK","type":"tool","id":"call_f27133d44bc74c7b830a4fdf","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 002\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`\n- Target type: spec-folder (fan-out lineage `scorer-attach`)\n- Artifact directory: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach`\n- Session: `fanout-scorer-attach-1794550137809-1ecgc7`, generation 1, lineage mode `new`\n- Dimension: security\n- Budget profile: verify (11-13 calls)\n- Prior findings: P0=0 P1=0 P2=2 (carried forward, still active)\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:44-241` (policy, class and owner tables)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs:454-500,1100-1230`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:677-698,882-939,1103-1170`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-status.ts:155-230`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:505-614`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/README.md:105-128`\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/install.md:1-60` and `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml:626-645` (context evidence for the derived class)\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\n1. **Hub-attached commands skip the no-edit gate the command scorer applies** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:353-388` -- `attachCommand` decides on the compiled route and the deep-loop effort wording only. It never consults `NO_EDIT_REQUEST`, while the command-row path in `lib/scorer/fusion.ts:677,887` refuses every command on a prompt that says \"no edits\", \"just show\" or \"do not change\". The same reader therefore gets no command from a scored command row but a mutating hub command from a single-mode route: `attachCommand('sk-doc', <sk-create-skill route>, 'explain the create skill flow, no edits')` returns `/create:skill`, whose class is `mutates` and whose policy is `start` (`command-attach.ts:66,129`).\n   Finding class: security / safety-of-offering-a-mutating-command\n   Scope proof: the guard would belong in `lib/command-attach.ts` (scorer-attach scope); its absence is reachable from `enrichCompiledRoutes` (`handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:472-479`), which runs on every hub recommendation.\n   Affected surface hints: hook brief command offer, recommend output `command`/`policy`, mutating `/create:*` commands\n   Case: a prompt that explicitly asks for an explanation with no edits and a compiled `sk-doc` route that names the `sk-create-skill` mode yields `sk-doc → /create:skill (start)`; no-edit wording is expected to suppress a mutating offer, as it does on the scorer path.\n   Mitigation in place: `start` means the command's setup asks before writing, and no `run` command in the shipped table has a writing class (executed proof below). Reach needs the compiled sk-doc route to name the create-skill mode, which is the route's own job for a create-skill prompt; the route was not executed here, so reach is stated, not proven.\n   Upgrade trigger: promote to P1 if the compiled `sk-doc` route returns `action=route, selectionKind=single, workflowMode=sk-create-skill` for an explicit no-edit prompt, or if a future mode maps to a `run` + mutating command.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `spec_code` | core | partial | Policy ladder `derivePolicy` (`derive-command-bridges.cjs:489-497`) matches README §8 step for step. |\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | pending | No packet checklist claims were in this iteration's focus. |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pending | Feature-catalog claims about policy and mutating classes were confirmed but the catalog pass is iteration 3. |\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- `derivePolicy` order: `ask_first` → `ask`; doctor + `mutates` → `ask`; `read-only` → `run`;\n  `add-only` + `write_scope=spec-folder` → `run`; otherwise `start` (`derive-command-bridges.cjs:489-497`).\n  README §8 reproduces the same five steps (`command-bridges/README.md:120-127`).\n- Executed check over the shipped table: 56 `COMMAND_ROWS`, **0** rows with policy `run` and a writing\n  class, **0** `run` + `mutates` rows, **0** policy mismatches between `TRACKED_COMMANDS` and the\n  generated `COMMAND_POLICIES` map.\n- `/doctor:install` is derived `run` from `mutating: read-only` (`_routes.yaml:631`), and the command\n  doc states it writes nothing and prints the writing commands for the operator\n  (`install.md:5`). The most dangerous-sounding `run` row is therefore correctly read-only.\n- Doctor hand-off safety: `runnableDoctorBridgeId` admits only a row whose policy is `run`\n  (`fusion.ts:1103-1110`), so a doctor route classed `mutates` can only reach the reader as\n  `/doctor:helper`, never by name.\n- Holdout hygiene: the only holdout vocabulary in this lineage's scope is the validate output schema,\n  which exposes `holdout_top1` as a matched/total/top1 slice\n  (`advisor-tool-schemas.ts:511-520,588-590`) and no per-row text. `lib/command-attach.ts`,\n  `handlers/advisor-status.ts`, `derive-command-bridges.cjs` and the command-bridge JSON contain no\n  holdout, corpus or prompt-row path. No holdout prompt text was read in this iteration.\n\n## Operator Focus Coverage\n\n- Mutating-command safety: executed proof that no `run` policy carries a writing class, plus the\n  deriver ladder and the install-guide cross-check; one P2 gap recorded for the hub-attach path.\n- Holdout hygiene: this lineage's surface is clean (count-only schema slices, no corpus path). The\n  tune/fix/report implementations that do touch splits live in\n  `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/*` and belong to the `accuracy-runner` lineage — named here as an\n  out-of-scope boundary, not asserted clean.\n- Six runtimes: `CommandRow` and `TrackedCommand` carry no runtime key\n  (`command-attach.ts:48-62`), so policy and class are runtime-agnostic by construction. Nothing in\n  this iteration diverges by runtime.\n- Docs that disagree with code: deferred to iteration 3.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- `TRACKED_COMMANDS` has 63 keys while `COMMAND_POLICIES` has 52: the 11 commands with no scorer row\n  (`/create:benchmark`, `/create:skill-parent`, `/deep:ai-council`, `/design:*`, …) carry their policy\n  in `TRACKED_COMMANDS`, and every consumer reads that map. Confirmed the two maps never disagree\n  where both hold a key (executed comparison).\n- `command-doctor-deep-loop` is `run` + `add-only` and writes a state file under the active spec\n  folder. Read as intended: the policy ladder explicitly allows a spec-folder-confined add-only route\n  to run, and it writes no source.\n- The doctor route manifest was read as context only; its content belongs to another lineage.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- Policy derivation and its documentation agree exactly (five-step ladder, same order, same outcomes).\n- No shipped command is both `run` and writing; a mutating command is `ask` (doctor) or `start`\n  (metadata), so every mutating offer still asks before writing.\n- The doctor hand-off never surfaces a mutating route by name.\n- Holdout rows are not reachable from this lineage's read paths, and the validate schema returns\n  counts only.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- \"`/doctor:install` is a mutating command mislabelled read-only\": ruled out against `install.md:5`\n  and the route's `gate3_location` n/a — it is a guide that prints commands.\n- \"A doctor route classed `mutates` can be offered by name through the helper hand-off\": ruled out by\n  the `policy === 'run'` filter in `runnableDoctorBridgeId`.\n- \"`COMMAND_POLICIES` and `TRACKED_COMMANDS` disagree\": ruled out by executed comparison (0 mismatches).\n- \"Holdout rows leak through `advisor_status`\": ruled out — the status surface reports vector counts,\n  not prompts.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: traceability\n- Focus area: docs that describe command surfacing versus the generated tables — the 45-row claim, the\n  runtime coverage sentence, and the feature-catalog claims about `MODE_COMMANDS`\n- Reason: the operator focus names docs that disagree with code, and two doc files were edited in the\n  same change as the generated tables\n- Rotation status: next dimension in the risk order\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: security was productive; carry the `COMMAND_POLICIES` dead-export\n  observation into maintainability\n- Required evidence: the doc line, the generated data line, and a count taken from the artifact\n\nReview verdict: PASS\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach/iterations/iteration-002.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach/iterations/iteration-002.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach/iterations/iteration-002.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Iteration 002\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`\\n- Target type: spec-folder (fan-out lineage `scorer-attach`)\\n- Artifact directory: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach`\\n- Session: `fanout-scorer-attach-1794550137809-1ecgc7`, generation 1, lineage mode `new`\\n- Dimension: security\\n- Budget profile: verify (11-13 calls)\\n- Prior findings: P0=0 P1=0 P2=2 (carried forward, still active)\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:44-241` (policy, class and owner tables)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs:454-500,1100-1230`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:677-698,882-939,1103-1170`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-status.ts:155-230`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:505-614`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/README.md:105-128`\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/install.md:1-60` and `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml:626-645` (context evidence for the derived class)\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\n1. **Hub-attached commands skip the no-edit gate the command scorer applies** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:353-388` -- `attachCommand` decides on the compiled route and the deep-loop effort wording only. It never consults `NO_EDIT_REQUEST`, while the command-row path in `lib/scorer/fusion.ts:677,887` refuses every command on a prompt that says \\\"no edits\\\", \\\"just show\\\" or \\\"do not change\\\". The same reader therefore gets no command from a scored command row but a mutating hub command from a single-mode route: `attachCommand('sk-doc', <sk-create-skill route>, 'explain the create skill flow, no edits')` returns `/create:skill`, whose class is `mutates` and whose policy is `start` (`command-attach.ts:66,129`).\\n   Finding class: security / safety-of-offering-a-mutating-command\\n   Scope proof: the guard would belong in `lib/command-attach.ts` (scorer-attach scope); its absence is reachable from `enrichCompiledRoutes` (`handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:472-479`), which runs on every hub recommendation.\\n   Affected surface hints: hook brief command offer, recommend output `command`/`policy`, mutating `/create:*` commands\\n   Case: a prompt that explicitly asks for an explanation with no edits and a compiled `sk-doc` route that names the `sk-create-skill` mode yields `sk-doc → /create:skill (start)`; no-edit wording is expected to suppress a mutating offer, as it does on the scorer path.\\n   Mitigation in place: `start` means the command's setup asks before writing, and no `run` command in the shipped table has a writing class (executed proof below). Reach needs the compiled sk-doc route to name the create-skill mode, which is the route's own job for a create-skill prompt; the route was not executed here, so reach is stated, not proven.\\n   Upgrade trigger: promote to P1 if the compiled `sk-doc` route returns `action=route, selectionKind=single, workflowMode=sk-create-skill` for an explicit no-edit prompt, or if a future mode maps to a `run` + mutating command.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Evidence |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| `spec_code` | core | partial | Policy ladder `derivePolicy` (`derive-command-bridges.cjs:489-497`) matches README §8 step for step. |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | pending | No packet checklist claims were in this iteration's focus. |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pending | Feature-catalog claims about policy and mutating classes were confirmed but the catalog pass is iteration 3. |\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- `derivePolicy` order: `ask_first` → `ask`; doctor + `mutates` → `ask`; `read-only` → `run`;\\n  `add-only` + `write_scope=spec-folder` → `run`; otherwise `start` (`derive-command-bridges.cjs:489-497`).\\n  README §8 reproduces the same five steps (`command-bridges/README.md:120-127`).\\n- Executed check over the shipped table: 56 `COMMAND_ROWS`, **0** rows with policy `run` and a writing\\n  class, **0** `run` + `mutates` rows, **0** policy mismatches between `TRACKED_COMMANDS` and the\\n  generated `COMMAND_POLICIES` map.\\n- `/doctor:install` is derived `run` from `mutating: read-only` (`_routes.yaml:631`), and the command\\n  doc states it writes nothing and prints the writing commands for the operator\\n  (`install.md:5`). The most dangerous-sounding `run` row is therefore correctly read-only.\\n- Doctor hand-off safety: `runnableDoctorBridgeId` admits only a row whose policy is `run`\\n  (`fusion.ts:1103-1110`), so a doctor route classed `mutates` can only reach the reader as\\n  `/doctor:helper`, never by name.\\n- Holdout hygiene: the only holdout vocabulary in this lineage's scope is the validate output schema,\\n  which exposes `holdout_top1` as a matched/total/top1 slice\\n  (`advisor-tool-schemas.ts:511-520,588-590`) and no per-row text. `lib/command-attach.ts`,\\n  `handlers/advisor-status.ts`, `derive-command-bridges.cjs` and the command-bridge JSON contain no\\n  holdout, corpus or prompt-row path. No holdout prompt text was read in this iteration.\\n\\n## Operator Focus Coverage\\n\\n- Mutating-command safety: executed proof that no `run` policy carries a writing class, plus the\\n  deriver ladder and the install-guide cross-check; one P2 gap recorded for the hub-attach path.\\n- Holdout hygiene: this lineage's surface is clean (count-only schema slices, no corpus path). The\\n  tune/fix/report implementations that do touch splits live in\\n  `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/*` and belong to the `accuracy-runner` lineage — named here as an\\n  out-of-scope boundary, not asserted clean.\\n- Six runtimes: `CommandRow` and `TrackedCommand` carry no runtime key\\n  (`command-attach.ts:48-62`), so policy and class are runtime-agnostic by construction. Nothing in\\n  this iteration diverges by runtime.\\n- Docs that disagree with code: deferred to iteration 3.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- `TRACKED_COMMANDS` has 63 keys while `COMMAND_POLICIES` has 52: the 11 commands with no scorer row\\n  (`/create:benchmark`, `/create:skill-parent`, `/deep:ai-council`, `/design:*`, …) carry their policy\\n  in `TRACKED_COMMANDS`, and every consumer reads that map. Confirmed the two maps never disagree\\n  where both hold a key (executed comparison).\\n- `command-doctor-deep-loop` is `run` + `add-only` and writes a state file under the active spec\\n  folder. Read as intended: the policy ladder explicitly allows a spec-folder-confined add-only route\\n  to run, and it writes no source.\\n- The doctor route manifest was read as context only; its content belongs to another lineage.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- Policy derivation and its documentation agree exactly (five-step ladder, same order, same outcomes).\\n- No shipped command is both `run` and writing; a mutating command is `ask` (doctor) or `start`\\n  (metadata), so every mutating offer still asks before writing.\\n- The doctor hand-off never surfaces a mutating route by name.\\n- Holdout rows are not reachable from this lineage's read paths, and the validate schema returns\\n  counts only.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- \\\"`/doctor:install` is a mutating command mislabelled read-only\\\": ruled out against `install.md:5`\\n  and the route's `gate3_location` n/a — it is a guide that prints commands.\\n- \\\"A doctor route classed `mutates` can be offered by name through the helper hand-off\\\": ruled out by\\n  the `policy === 'run'` filter in `runnableDoctorBridgeId`.\\n- \\\"`COMMAND_POLICIES` and `TRACKED_COMMANDS` disagree\\\": ruled out by executed comparison (0 mismatches).\\n- \\\"Holdout rows leak through `advisor_status`\\\": ruled out — the status surface reports vector counts,\\n  not prompts.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: traceability\\n- Focus area: docs that describe command surfacing versus the generated tables — the 45-row claim, the\\n  runtime coverage sentence, and the feature-catalog claims about `MODE_COMMANDS`\\n- Reason: the operator focus names docs that disagree with code, and two doc files were edited in the\\n  same change as the generated tables\\n- Rotation status: next dimension in the risk order\\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: security was productive; carry the `COMMAND_POLICIES` dead-export\\n  observation into maintainability\\n- Required evidence: the doc line, the generated data line, and a count taken from the artifact\\n\\nReview verdict: PASS\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach/iterations/iteration-002.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794551486861,"end":1794551513099}}}}
