{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794551705581,"sessionID":"ses_e2c7999e1ffeYcD6BDSYeMhQPJ","part":{"partID":"prt_1d39dee72002JH5mE0YIiU51ot","sessionID":"ses_e2c7999e1ffeYcD6BDSYeMhQPJ","messageID":"msg_1d39ddf29001qHpWV2rxSnIGZu","type":"tool","id":"call_11e22cf90b2c4da989931b27","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research; sed -n '270,305p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts"},"output":"// `AdvisorScoringOptions.affordances` (see `lib/scorer/types.ts:94`) is a\n// COMPILE-TIME-ONLY internal seam used by the scorer fusion path. Affordance\n// evidence is sourced from compiled skill graph metadata via\n// `skill_graph_compiler.py` (which emits sanitized `derived.affordances[]`\n// nodes), not from public command input. Exposing `affordances` through this\n// request schema would re-introduce the prompt-stuffing surface that\n// `affordance-normalizer.ts` specifically defends against (URLs, emails,\n// instruction-shaped strings, free-form `description` fields). The public\n// `advisor_recommend` tool intentionally does NOT accept `affordances`.\n// Internal callers that need request-local affordance scoring should invoke\n// `scoreAdvisorPrompt` directly with `AdvisorScoringOptions.affordances`.\n// advisor_recommend routes on at most this many prompt characters. A caller holding a\n// longer prompt sends its head, so a long prompt is routed rather than refused.\nexport const ADVISOR_PROMPT_MAX_CHARS = 10_000;\n\nexport const AdvisorRecommendInputSchema = z.object({\n  // workspaceRoot must resolve under the allowed prefix set.\n  workspaceRoot: BoundedWorkspaceRootSchema.optional(),\n  prompt: z.string().min(1).max(ADVISOR_PROMPT_MAX_CHARS),\n  options: z.object({\n    topK: z.number().int().min(1).max(10).optional(),\n    includeAttribution: z.boolean().optional(),\n    includeAbstainReasons: z.boolean().optional(),\n    confidenceThreshold: z.number().min(0).max(1).optional(),\n    uncertaintyThreshold: z.number().min(0).max(1).optional(),\n    includeCompiledRoute: z.boolean().optional(),\n    // Limits the per-hub route lookup to the first recommendation, for a caller\n    // on a tight time budget that acts on the top pick alone.\n    compiledRouteTopOnly: z.boolean().optional(),\n    // Forwarded to the compiled-route front door as --surface-hint; a value\n    // that names no known surface is ignored there.\n    surfaceHint: z.string().min(1).max(64).optional(),\n  }).strict().optional(),\n}).strict();\n\nexport const AdvisorRecommendationSchema = z.object({\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"// `AdvisorScoringOptions.affordances` (see `lib/scorer/types.ts:94`) is a\n// COMPILE-TIME-ONLY internal seam used by the scorer fusion path. Affordance\n// evidence is sourced from compiled skill graph metadata via\n// `skill_graph_compiler.py` (which emits sanitized `derived.affordances[]`\n// nodes), not from public command input. Exposing `affordances` through this\n// request schema would re-introduce the prompt-stuffing surface that\n// `affordance-normalizer.ts` specifically defends against (URLs, emails,\n// instruction-shaped strings, free-form `description` fields). The public\n// `advisor_recommend` tool intentionally does NOT accept `affordances`.\n// Internal callers that need request-local affordance scoring should invoke\n// `scoreAdvisorPrompt` directly with `AdvisorScoringOptions.affordances`.\n// advisor_recommend routes on at most this many prompt characters. A caller holding a\n// longer prompt sends its head, so a long prompt is routed rather than refused.\nexport const ADVISOR_PROMPT_MAX_CHARS = 10_000;\n\nexport const AdvisorRecommendInputSchema = z.object({\n  // workspaceRoot must resolve under the allowed prefix set.\n  workspaceRoot: BoundedWorkspaceRootSchema.optional(),\n  prompt: z.string().min(1).max(ADVISOR_PROMPT_MAX_CHARS),\n  options: z.object({\n    topK: z.number().int().min(1).max(10).optional(),\n    includeAttribution: z.boolean().optional(),\n    includeAbstainReasons: z.boolean().optional(),\n    confidenceThreshold: z.number().min(0).max(1).optional(),\n    uncertaintyThreshold: z.number().min(0).max(1).optional(),\n    includeCompiledRoute: z.boolean().optional(),\n    // Limits the per-hub route lookup to the first recommendation, for a caller\n    // on a tight time budget that acts on the top pick alone.\n    compiledRouteTopOnly: z.boolean().optional(),\n    // Forwarded to the compiled-route front door as --surface-hint; a value\n    // that names no known surface is ignored there.\n    surfaceHint: z.string().min(1).max(64).optional(),\n  }).strict().optional(),\n}).strict();\n\nexport const AdvisorRecommendationSchema = z.object({\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research; sed -n '270,305p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts\"}"},"time":{"start":1794551705202,"end":1794551705581}}}}
