{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794551785110,"sessionID":"ses_e2c7999e1ffeYcD6BDSYeMhQPJ","part":{"partID":"prt_1d39ea932002szaLUgMdDcs53V","sessionID":"ses_e2c7999e1ffeYcD6BDSYeMhQPJ","messageID":"msg_1d39e893a001F6AiBGylMnOcHE","type":"tool","id":"call_483ee59f8bff4f0480c9c48f","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research; grep -rn \"COMMAND_POLICIES\" --include=*.ts --include=*.cjs --include=*.mjs --include=*.js --include=*.md . 2>/dev/null | grep -v node_modules | grep -v \"/specs/\" | head -20; echo \"=== fusion dead if ===\"; sed -n '745,756p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts"},"output":"./.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md:45:`lib/command-attach.ts` is the single source for the values. Its generated `COMMAND_ROWS` block maps each id a scorer can return, whether the TypeScript id, the Python id or the entry id, to `{ command, policy?, ownerSkillId }`, and `commandRowFor(id)` reads it with an own-key check so an inherited name such as `constructor` never resolves to a row. `publicRecommendation()` in `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` looks one up for the recommendation's own id and copies its `command`, its `policy` when present and its `ownerSkillId`, and it forwards the scorer's `kind`. An id with no row adds none of the three. A command attached through the compiled route takes its `policy` from `COMMAND_POLICIES[command]` because that generated table is keyed by runnable string, and it takes no `ownerSkillId` because the recommendation already names the hub.\n./.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/dist/runtime/lib/command-attach.js:100:export const COMMAND_POLICIES = {\n./.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs:1218:    \"export const COMMAND_POLICIES: Readonly<Record<string, 'run' | 'start' | 'ask'>> = {\",\n./.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/README.md:50:The deriver also updates generated projection blocks in the live TypeScript and Python scoring sources. Its `GENERATED COMMAND ROWS` block in `lib/command-attach.ts` holds `COMMAND_ROWS`, one row per id a scorer can return for an enabled entry, covering the entry id and every enabled runtime id. Each row carries the runnable slash command, its derived policy and the owning skill. The same block holds `COMMAND_POLICIES`, one policy per runnable string, so a surface that attaches a command can name its policy without a second lookup. It writes the `MODE_COMMANDS` block into the same file, one row per hub mode that names a command, and fails when a mode names a command with no file under `.skilled/commands/`. The same block also holds `TRACKED_COMMANDS`, one row per tracked command keyed by its runnable string, emitted for every bridge entry whether or not the bridge is active. Each TypeScript bridge in `lib/scorer/projection.ts` carries an `ownerSkill`, the skill that owns its command. The generated JSON and generated source blocks are outputs, not hand-edited inputs.\n./.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:123:export const COMMAND_POLICIES: Readonly<Record<string, 'run' | 'start' | 'ask'>> = {\n=== fusion dead if ===\nfunction primaryIntentBonus(\n  promptLower: string,\n  recommendation: AdvisorScoredRecommendation,\n): number {\n  const R = SCORING_CALIBRATION.routing;\n  if (/\\bsemantic (code )?search\\b/.test(promptLower)) {\n  }\n  if (/\\bdeep[- ]review\\b/.test(promptLower)) {\n    if (recommendation.skill === 'sk-code') {\n      return AUTHORS_CODE.test(promptLower) ? R.deepReviewCodeAuthoringSkCodeBonus : R.deepReviewSkCodeReviewPenalty;\n    }\n  }\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"./.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md:45:`lib/command-attach.ts` is the single source for the values. Its generated `COMMAND_ROWS` block maps each id a scorer can return, whether the TypeScript id, the Python id or the entry id, to `{ command, policy?, ownerSkillId }`, and `commandRowFor(id)` reads it with an own-key check so an inherited name such as `constructor` never resolves to a row. `publicRecommendation()` in `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` looks one up for the recommendation's own id and copies its `command`, its `policy` when present and its `ownerSkillId`, and it forwards the scorer's `kind`. An id with no row adds none of the three. A command attached through the compiled route takes its `policy` from `COMMAND_POLICIES[command]` because that generated table is keyed by runnable string, and it takes no `ownerSkillId` because the recommendation already names the hub.\n./.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/dist/runtime/lib/command-attach.js:100:export const COMMAND_POLICIES = {\n./.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs:1218:    \"export const COMMAND_POLICIES: Readonly<Record<string, 'run' | 'start' | 'ask'>> = {\",\n./.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/README.md:50:The deriver also updates generated projection blocks in the live TypeScript and Python scoring sources. Its `GENERATED COMMAND ROWS` block in `lib/command-attach.ts` holds `COMMAND_ROWS`, one row per id a scorer can return for an enabled entry, covering the entry id and every enabled runtime id. Each row carries the runnable slash command, its derived policy and the owning skill. The same block holds `COMMAND_POLICIES`, one policy per runnable string, so a surface that attaches a command can name its policy without a second lookup. It writes the `MODE_COMMANDS` block into the same file, one row per hub mode that names a command, and fails when a mode names a command with no file under `.skilled/commands/`. The same block also holds `TRACKED_COMMANDS`, one row per tracked command keyed by its runnable string, emitted for every bridge entry whether or not the bridge is active. Each TypeScript bridge in `lib/scorer/projection.ts` carries an `ownerSkill`, the skill that owns its command. The generated JSON and generated source blocks are outputs, not hand-edited inputs.\n./.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:123:export const COMMAND_POLICIES: Readonly<Record<string, 'run' | 'start' | 'ask'>> = {\n=== fusion dead if ===\nfunction primaryIntentBonus(\n  promptLower: string,\n  recommendation: AdvisorScoredRecommendation,\n): number {\n  const R = SCORING_CALIBRATION.routing;\n  if (/\\bsemantic (code )?search\\b/.test(promptLower)) {\n  }\n  if (/\\bdeep[- ]review\\b/.test(promptLower)) {\n    if (recommendation.skill === 'sk-code') {\n      return AUTHORS_CODE.test(promptLower) ? R.deepReviewCodeAuthoringSkCodeBonus : R.deepReviewSkCodeReviewPenalty;\n    }\n  }\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research; grep -rn \\\"COMMAND_POLICIES\\\" --include=*.ts --include=*.cjs --include=*.mjs --include=*.js --include=*.md . 2>/dev/null | grep -v node_modules | grep -v \\\"/specs/\\\" | head -20; echo \\\"=== fusion dead if ===\\\"; sed -n '745,756p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts\"}"},"time":{"start":1794551753010,"end":1794551785110}}}}
