{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794551834773,"sessionID":"ses_e2c7999e1ffeYcD6BDSYeMhQPJ","part":{"partID":"prt_1d39f84f8001WL9OR0Qbz3cFTB","sessionID":"ses_e2c7999e1ffeYcD6BDSYeMhQPJ","messageID":"msg_1d39f66ed001J5vT2pKznlBlHd","type":"tool","id":"call_e36e5b5faff74255897b1306","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 004\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`\n- Target type: spec-folder (fan-out lineage `scorer-attach`)\n- Artifact directory: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach`\n- Session: `fanout-scorer-attach-1794550137809-1ecgc7`, generation 1, lineage mode `new`\n- Dimension: maintainability\n- Budget profile: scan (9-11 calls)\n- Prior findings: P0=0 P1=0 P2=5 (carried forward, still active)\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:44-241`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:13,449-482`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs:1180-1230`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/README.md:50-54,128`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:745-790`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md:45` (context evidence; `render-hooks-plugin` scope)\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\n1. **`COMMAND_POLICIES` is generated, drift-guarded and documented as the attach-path policy lookup, but no code reads it** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:123-176` -- the generated block holds 52 policy rows and the deriver regenerates it on every run (`derive-command-bridges.cjs:1218`), yet a repository-wide reference search finds only its declaration, the generator, the built `dist` copy and prose. The one attach path reads the policy from `TRACKED_COMMANDS[command].policy` instead (`handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:478`), so the table is a second source of truth that nothing consumes. The command-bridges README says the block exists \"so a surface that attaches a command can name its policy without a second lookup\" (`command-bridges/README.md:50`), and a feature-catalog page in another lineage's scope states the opposite of the code (\"takes its `policy` from `COMMAND_POLICIES[command]`\", `feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md:45`).\n   Finding class: maintainability / dead generated surface + contradictory documentation\n   Scope proof: the dead block and its consumer are both scorer-attach paths (`lib/command-attach.ts`, `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts`); the catalog page is cited as context only and is not filed against, because `render-hooks-plugin` owns it.\n   Affected surface hints: generated blocks and their drift guard, attach-path policy source, two prose surfaces\n   Case: a maintainer corrects a policy in the generated `commandPolicies` record or in `COMMAND_POLICIES` and ships it; nothing changes, because the attach path reads `TRACKED_COMMANDS`. A reader of the catalog believes the opposite, so the two docs cannot both be right.\n   Evidence: generated block at lines 123-176; consumer at `advisor-recommend.ts:478`; README sentence at `command-bridges/README.md:50`; catalog sentence at `feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md:45`; repository-wide search for `COMMAND_POLICIES` returns no import site.\n   Downgrade trigger: none at P2; the two maps currently agree in value (iteration 2 executed comparison), so this is a cost and a contradiction, not a live wrong policy.\n\n2. **Dead empty conditional in `primaryIntentBonus`** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:750-751` -- the branch tests `/\\bsemantic (code )?search\\b/` against the prompt and then returns nothing, so the test runs on every recommendation and changes no score. No other code depends on the branch's presence.\n   Finding class: maintainability / dead control flow\n   Scope proof: `lib/scorer/fusion.ts` is a scorer-attach scope entry; the branch is inside the scoring path consumed by every recommendation.\n   Affected surface hints: `primaryIntentBonus`, per-recommendation scoring cost, reviewer confidence in the rule table\n   Case: a reader of the bonus ladder sees a rule for semantic-search prompts and assumes semantic-search prompts get a bonus; they get none, and the next rule decides. Removing the branch changes no output.\n   Evidence: the empty block read at lines 750-751; no assignment or return inside it.\n   Downgrade trigger: none at P2; pre-existing rather than introduced here, and cosmetic in impact.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `spec_code` | core | partial | The generated policy block's documented role does not match its only consumer (recorded above). |\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | partial | No packet checklist claim covers generated-block consumption. |\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | pass | Carried from iteration 3 (36/36 owner tags match). |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | partial | Carried from iteration 3 (architecture prose omits `dsh`). |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | partial | Both catalog pages describe command surfaces; the cli-surface page contradicts the code's policy source (context, other lineage) and the scorer-fusion page carries the 45-row drift. |\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | notApplicable | No playbook path is part of this surface. |\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:13` imports `TRACKED_COMMANDS`; the file does not import\n  `COMMAND_POLICIES`.\n- `derive-command-bridges.cjs:1180-1215` emits both `TRACKED_COMMANDS` (with `policy`) and\n  `COMMAND_POLICIES`, so the same fact is generated twice from one policy record.\n- `command-bridges-drift-guard.vitest.ts` pins the regenerated file byte for byte, so the dead block is\n  actively maintained rather than merely stale.\n\n## Operator Focus Coverage\n\n- Docs that disagree with code: the dead table is the code-side cause of a doc contradiction; the\n  catalog page itself belongs to `render-hooks-plugin` and is named, not filed against.\n- Six runtimes: no runtime branch is added by either finding.\n- Mutating-command safety: unchanged — the two policy maps agree in value today, so the dead table does\n  not currently mis-state a policy.\n- Holdout hygiene: no holdout path is touched by this iteration.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Deleting `COMMAND_POLICIES` would also need the deriver emitter and the drift-guard expectation\n  updated in the same change; wiring the consumer to it is the smaller change. Either fix is a\n  one-owner decision, recorded here rather than executed (review is observation-only).\n- The empty conditional is pre-existing; reporting it is still actionable because the file is in scope\n  and the branch is one line.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- `COMMAND_ROWS` and `TRACKED_COMMANDS` currently agree wherever both hold a key (iteration 2 executed\n  comparison, 0 mismatches), so the duplicate tables have not drifted in value.\n- The deriver emits both maps from one policy record, so a generator-level fix keeps them aligned.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- \"`COMMAND_POLICIES` is read through a namespace or dynamic access\": ruled out — a repository-wide\n  search finds no import site and no `command-attach` namespace import.\n- \"The empty conditional is a stub for a planned rule\": ruled out as an assumption; no comment, no\n  ticket reference, and no test asserts a semantic-search bonus.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: cross-reference / adversarial recheck\n- Focus area: revalidate the five active P2 findings against current file content, confirm the\n  convergence signal, and check that no finding was filed outside the lineage's scope\n- Reason: last iteration; the cap and the convergence rule meet here\n- Rotation status: all four dimensions covered; this is the stabilization pass\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: maintainability was productive; no blocked approaches\n- Required evidence: a reread of every cited line and a scope audit of the lineage directory\n\nReview verdict: PASS\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach/iterations/iteration-004.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach/iterations/iteration-004.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach/iterations/iteration-004.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Iteration 004\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`\\n- Target type: spec-folder (fan-out lineage `scorer-attach`)\\n- Artifact directory: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach`\\n- Session: `fanout-scorer-attach-1794550137809-1ecgc7`, generation 1, lineage mode `new`\\n- Dimension: maintainability\\n- Budget profile: scan (9-11 calls)\\n- Prior findings: P0=0 P1=0 P2=5 (carried forward, still active)\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:44-241`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:13,449-482`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs:1180-1230`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/README.md:50-54,128`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:745-790`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md:45` (context evidence; `render-hooks-plugin` scope)\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\n1. **`COMMAND_POLICIES` is generated, drift-guarded and documented as the attach-path policy lookup, but no code reads it** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:123-176` -- the generated block holds 52 policy rows and the deriver regenerates it on every run (`derive-command-bridges.cjs:1218`), yet a repository-wide reference search finds only its declaration, the generator, the built `dist` copy and prose. The one attach path reads the policy from `TRACKED_COMMANDS[command].policy` instead (`handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:478`), so the table is a second source of truth that nothing consumes. The command-bridges README says the block exists \\\"so a surface that attaches a command can name its policy without a second lookup\\\" (`command-bridges/README.md:50`), and a feature-catalog page in another lineage's scope states the opposite of the code (\\\"takes its `policy` from `COMMAND_POLICIES[command]`\\\", `feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md:45`).\\n   Finding class: maintainability / dead generated surface + contradictory documentation\\n   Scope proof: the dead block and its consumer are both scorer-attach paths (`lib/command-attach.ts`, `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts`); the catalog page is cited as context only and is not filed against, because `render-hooks-plugin` owns it.\\n   Affected surface hints: generated blocks and their drift guard, attach-path policy source, two prose surfaces\\n   Case: a maintainer corrects a policy in the generated `commandPolicies` record or in `COMMAND_POLICIES` and ships it; nothing changes, because the attach path reads `TRACKED_COMMANDS`. A reader of the catalog believes the opposite, so the two docs cannot both be right.\\n   Evidence: generated block at lines 123-176; consumer at `advisor-recommend.ts:478`; README sentence at `command-bridges/README.md:50`; catalog sentence at `feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md:45`; repository-wide search for `COMMAND_POLICIES` returns no import site.\\n   Downgrade trigger: none at P2; the two maps currently agree in value (iteration 2 executed comparison), so this is a cost and a contradiction, not a live wrong policy.\\n\\n2. **Dead empty conditional in `primaryIntentBonus`** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:750-751` -- the branch tests `/\\\\bsemantic (code )?search\\\\b/` against the prompt and then returns nothing, so the test runs on every recommendation and changes no score. No other code depends on the branch's presence.\\n   Finding class: maintainability / dead control flow\\n   Scope proof: `lib/scorer/fusion.ts` is a scorer-attach scope entry; the branch is inside the scoring path consumed by every recommendation.\\n   Affected surface hints: `primaryIntentBonus`, per-recommendation scoring cost, reviewer confidence in the rule table\\n   Case: a reader of the bonus ladder sees a rule for semantic-search prompts and assumes semantic-search prompts get a bonus; they get none, and the next rule decides. Removing the branch changes no output.\\n   Evidence: the empty block read at lines 750-751; no assignment or return inside it.\\n   Downgrade trigger: none at P2; pre-existing rather than introduced here, and cosmetic in impact.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Evidence |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| `spec_code` | core | partial | The generated policy block's documented role does not match its only consumer (recorded above). |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | partial | No packet checklist claim covers generated-block consumption. |\\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | pass | Carried from iteration 3 (36/36 owner tags match). |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | partial | Carried from iteration 3 (architecture prose omits `dsh`). |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | partial | Both catalog pages describe command surfaces; the cli-surface page contradicts the code's policy source (context, other lineage) and the scorer-fusion page carries the 45-row drift. |\\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | notApplicable | No playbook path is part of this surface. |\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:13` imports `TRACKED_COMMANDS`; the file does not import\\n  `COMMAND_POLICIES`.\\n- `derive-command-bridges.cjs:1180-1215` emits both `TRACKED_COMMANDS` (with `policy`) and\\n  `COMMAND_POLICIES`, so the same fact is generated twice from one policy record.\\n- `command-bridges-drift-guard.vitest.ts` pins the regenerated file byte for byte, so the dead block is\\n  actively maintained rather than merely stale.\\n\\n## Operator Focus Coverage\\n\\n- Docs that disagree with code: the dead table is the code-side cause of a doc contradiction; the\\n  catalog page itself belongs to `render-hooks-plugin` and is named, not filed against.\\n- Six runtimes: no runtime branch is added by either finding.\\n- Mutating-command safety: unchanged — the two policy maps agree in value today, so the dead table does\\n  not currently mis-state a policy.\\n- Holdout hygiene: no holdout path is touched by this iteration.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- Deleting `COMMAND_POLICIES` would also need the deriver emitter and the drift-guard expectation\\n  updated in the same change; wiring the consumer to it is the smaller change. Either fix is a\\n  one-owner decision, recorded here rather than executed (review is observation-only).\\n- The empty conditional is pre-existing; reporting it is still actionable because the file is in scope\\n  and the branch is one line.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- `COMMAND_ROWS` and `TRACKED_COMMANDS` currently agree wherever both hold a key (iteration 2 executed\\n  comparison, 0 mismatches), so the duplicate tables have not drifted in value.\\n- The deriver emits both maps from one policy record, so a generator-level fix keeps them aligned.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- \\\"`COMMAND_POLICIES` is read through a namespace or dynamic access\\\": ruled out — a repository-wide\\n  search finds no import site and no `command-attach` namespace import.\\n- \\\"The empty conditional is a stub for a planned rule\\\": ruled out as an assumption; no comment, no\\n  ticket reference, and no test asserts a semantic-search bonus.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: cross-reference / adversarial recheck\\n- Focus area: revalidate the five active P2 findings against current file content, confirm the\\n  convergence signal, and check that no finding was filed outside the lineage's scope\\n- Reason: last iteration; the cap and the convergence rule meet here\\n- Rotation status: all four dimensions covered; this is the stabilization pass\\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: maintainability was productive; no blocked approaches\\n- Required evidence: a reread of every cited line and a scope audit of the lineage directory\\n\\nReview verdict: PASS\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach/iterations/iteration-004.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794551809272,"end":1794551834773}}}}
