{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794552033236,"sessionID":"ses_e2c7999e1ffeYcD6BDSYeMhQPJ","part":{"partID":"prt_1d3a27248001fq2RJ9GDLiZS3S","sessionID":"ses_e2c7999e1ffeYcD6BDSYeMhQPJ","messageID":"msg_1d3a25aad001kZCdImROnOeIur","type":"tool","id":"call_189a00fb52714005a90b3015","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Deep Review Report - scorer-attach lineage\n\n- Target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`\n- Lineage: `scorer-attach` (fan-out), session `fanout-scorer-attach-1794550137809-1ecgc7`, generation 1\n- Dimensions: correctness, security, traceability, maintainability\n- Iterations: 5 of 5 (convergence reached at the cap; `newFindingsRatio` 0.00 on the last pass)\n- Verdict: **PASS** with 7 active P2 advisories (`hasAdvisories = true`)\n\n## 1. Executive summary\n\nThe command-surfacing change holds up on the two questions that matter most. No shipped command is\nboth runnable without asking (`run`) and writing: an executed sweep of all 56 `COMMAND_ROWS` found 0\nsuch rows, the policy ladder in `derive-command-bridges.cjs` produces that result by construction,\nand the doctor hand-off refuses to name any mutating route. No holdout row is reachable from this\nlineage's surface: the validate schema exposes only matched/total/top1 slices, and no\ncommand-surfacing path reads a corpus file.\n\nSeven P2 advisories remain, all in two themes. Three are attach-path behaviour: the deep-loop effort\ngate accepts any `/deep:` mention rather than the command being attached, a document path such as\n`/create:skill.md` is read as a typed command, and the hub-attach path offers a mutating `/create:*`\ncommand on an explicit no-edit prompt where the scorer path refuses one. Three are doc-code drift: two\nsentences added by this change say 45 TypeScript-served command rows where the artifact holds 46, and\nthe runtime coverage sentence omits `dsh`. One is dead generated data: `COMMAND_POLICIES` is\nregenerated and drift-guarded but read by no code, while two prose surfaces disagree about whether it\nis the policy source. A seventh small advisory records a dead empty conditional on the scoring path.\n\nNone of these blocks release. The three attach-path advisories are wrong-offer risks, not wrong-write\nrisks, because every mutating command they can reach carries `start` or `ask`.\n\n## 2. Planning trigger\n\n- Required: no. There is no active P0 and no active P1, so the promotion gate is PASS.\n- Recommended: yes, as one small cleanup packet. Four of the seven advisories are one-line or\n  one-sentence fixes, and two of them (the doc counts) are corrections to text added in this change.\n- Not recommended: a remediation plan that reopens the command-surfacing design. The route-derived\n  attach contract, the policy ladder and the single-mode rule are sound.\n\n## 3. Active finding registry\n\n| Id | Severity | Dimension | Location | Title |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| R1-P2-001 | P2 | correctness | `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:385` | Deep-loop depth gate is satisfied by any typed `/deep:` prefix, not the attached command |\n| R1-P2-002 | P2 | correctness | `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:266` | Typed-command scan reads a document reference as the command |\n| R2-P2-001 | P2 | security | `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:353` | Hub-attached commands skip the no-edit gate the command scorer applies |\n| R3-P2-001 | P2 | traceability | `README.md:176` (also `feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md:26`) | Two docs added by this change state 45 TypeScript-served command rows; the artifact holds 46 |\n| R3-P2-002 | P2 | traceability | `ARCHITECTURE.md:142` | The runtime coverage sentence omits `dsh` while the canonical set and hook readers include it |\n| R4-P2-001 | P2 | maintainability | `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:123` | `COMMAND_POLICIES` is generated, drift-guarded and documented as the attach-path policy lookup, but no code reads it |\n| R4-P2-002 | P2 | maintainability | `runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:750` | Dead empty conditional in `primaryIntentBonus` |\n\nTotals: P0 0, P1 0, P2 7 active, 0 resolved, 0 repeated.\n\n## 4. Remediation workstreams\n\n**W1 - Attach-path guards** (R1-P2-001, R1-P2-002, R2-P2-001)\nReuse one predicate for \"the prompt asks for no change\" on the hub-attach path, the way\n`fusion.ts` already does for command rows; match a typed command only at a command boundary that\nrejects a trailing `.` path extension; and gate a deep-loop command on the command actually attached\n(or on a per-command effort table) rather than on the presence of `/deep:`.\nOwner: the advisor runtime. Size: one file plus tests. Risk: low — three narrow guards, all with a\nunit reproduction already in the iteration files.\n\n**W2 - Documentation truth** (R3-P2-001, R3-P2-002)\nCorrect the two 45-row sentences to 46 and add `dsh` to the runtime sentence (or state what the\nsentence is enumerating if it is deliberately narrower than the runtime label set).\nOwner: docs. Size: three lines. Risk: none.\n\n**W3 - Dead generated surface** (R4-P2-001)\nChoose one: delete `COMMAND_POLICIES` from the generated block and its emitter, or point\n`advisor-recommend.ts:478` at it and drop the duplicate policy from `TRACKED_COMMANDS`. The second is\nthe smaller diff and makes the two prose surfaces agree. The `render-hooks-plugin` catalog page that\nalready describes the second shape is another lineage's file, so a coordinated touch is needed if the\ndelete option is chosen.\nOwner: advisor runtime plus that doc's owner. Size: one emitter change and one consumer line, or a\ndelete plus drift-guard update. Risk: low.\n\n**W4 - Dead control flow** (R4-P2-002)\nDelete the empty `if` block in `primaryIntentBonus`. No expected-output change.\nOwner: advisor runtime. Size: two lines. Risk: none.\n\n## 5. Spec seed\n\nProposed acceptance criteria for a cleanup packet:\n\n1. A prompt containing only `/deep:<other-mode>` never attaches a deep command for a different mode.\n2. A prompt that cites a command document path (`/create:<name>.md`) attaches no command.\n3. A prompt matching the shared no-edit wording attaches no mutating command from either the scorer\n   path or the hub route path.\n4. The documented TypeScript-served command-row count equals `counts.typescriptActive` in\n   `command-bridges.generated.json`.\n5. The architecture runtime sentence names every runtime in `ADVISOR_RUNTIME_VALUES`, or states the\n   narrower enumeration it intends.\n6. No generated export in `command-attach.ts` lacks a runtime consumer, or its documented consumer is\n   the one that reads it.\n7. The scoring path contains no empty conditional.\n\n## 6. Plan seed\n\n1. Add the no-edit predicate to `attachCommand` and reuse the same regex constant as `fusion.ts`\n   (avoid a second copy).\n2. Tighten `typedCommandIn`'s end boundary so a `.` or a path separator after the command cancels the\n   match, keeping `-` as a continuation character.\n3. Replace the `includes('/deep:')` bypass with a check on the command returned for the routed mode.\n4. Update the two row-count sentences and the runtime sentence.\n5. Resolve `COMMAND_POLICIES`: wire the consumer or delete the block and its emitter.\n6. Delete the empty conditional.\n7. Add one regression test per changed behaviour, each failing on the old code for exactly one reason.\n\n## 7. Traceability status\n\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `spec_code` | core | partial | Four P2 deviations across the generated tables and their docs. |\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | partial | No packet checklist claim is contradicted; no claim covers the generated blocks. |\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | pass | 36 doctor bridge owners match their 17 router `skill_agent` tags, 0 mismatches. |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | partial | Seven runtime labels accepted; architecture prose omits `dsh`. |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | partial | Cosine 0.72 and margin 0.02 claims match the constants; the 45-row count does not. |\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | notApplicable | No playbook path in this surface. |\n\nResource Map Coverage Gate: skipped — no `resource-map.md` at init.\n\n## 8. Deferred items\n\n- Holdout-path hygiene for the `tune`, `fix` and report commands: the implementations live in\n  `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/*` and belong to the `accuracy-runner` lineage. This lineage\n  verified only that its own surface never reads or prints holdout rows, and read no holdout prompt\n  text (counts only).\n- Compiled-route mode selection for no-edit prompts: proving the reach of R2-P2-001 needs a write-safe\n  probe of `.skilled/bin/compiled-route.cjs --hub sk-doc`, which is outside this lineage's write-safe\n  scope.\n- The `feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md` sentence that names `COMMAND_POLICIES` as the\n  policy source: `render-hooks-plugin` owns that file; it was cited as context for R4-P2-001 and not\n  filed against.\n- Runtime-specific command rendering (the hook brief and the six runtime adapters): outside this\n  lineage; the runtime label set and the docs were checked, the renderers were not.\n\n## 9. Audit appendix\n\n- Iterations: `iterations/iteration-001.md` … `iteration-005.md`; deltas `deltas/iter-001.jsonl` …\n  `iter-005.jsonl`; each iteration recorded once through `append-mode-event.cjs` (ledger sequences\n  2-6, all exit 0) and reduced with `reduce-state.cjs`.\n- Evidence style: every finding cites `file:line`. Four findings were reproduced by executing the\n  shipped module with `node --experimental-strip-types`; four whole-table checks were executed\n  (`COMMAND_ROWS` policy/class sweep, policy-map agreement, `MODE_COMMANDS` file existence, doctor\n  owner tags).\n- Scope audit: every write resolved under\n  `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach`.\n  No review target, config, findings registry, dashboard, command, skill or mirror was hand-edited;\n  the registry and dashboard are reducer output.\n- Anti-sycophancy note: R2-P2-001 was tested against its own P1 promotion trigger in iteration 5 and\n  held at P2 because the reach condition was not proven.\n- Holdout handling: no holdout prompt text was read or printed in any iteration.\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach/review-report.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach/review-report.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach/review-report.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Deep Review Report - scorer-attach lineage\\n\\n- Target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`\\n- Lineage: `scorer-attach` (fan-out), session `fanout-scorer-attach-1794550137809-1ecgc7`, generation 1\\n- Dimensions: correctness, security, traceability, maintainability\\n- Iterations: 5 of 5 (convergence reached at the cap; `newFindingsRatio` 0.00 on the last pass)\\n- Verdict: **PASS** with 7 active P2 advisories (`hasAdvisories = true`)\\n\\n## 1. Executive summary\\n\\nThe command-surfacing change holds up on the two questions that matter most. No shipped command is\\nboth runnable without asking (`run`) and writing: an executed sweep of all 56 `COMMAND_ROWS` found 0\\nsuch rows, the policy ladder in `derive-command-bridges.cjs` produces that result by construction,\\nand the doctor hand-off refuses to name any mutating route. No holdout row is reachable from this\\nlineage's surface: the validate schema exposes only matched/total/top1 slices, and no\\ncommand-surfacing path reads a corpus file.\\n\\nSeven P2 advisories remain, all in two themes. Three are attach-path behaviour: the deep-loop effort\\ngate accepts any `/deep:` mention rather than the command being attached, a document path such as\\n`/create:skill.md` is read as a typed command, and the hub-attach path offers a mutating `/create:*`\\ncommand on an explicit no-edit prompt where the scorer path refuses one. Three are doc-code drift: two\\nsentences added by this change say 45 TypeScript-served command rows where the artifact holds 46, and\\nthe runtime coverage sentence omits `dsh`. One is dead generated data: `COMMAND_POLICIES` is\\nregenerated and drift-guarded but read by no code, while two prose surfaces disagree about whether it\\nis the policy source. A seventh small advisory records a dead empty conditional on the scoring path.\\n\\nNone of these blocks release. The three attach-path advisories are wrong-offer risks, not wrong-write\\nrisks, because every mutating command they can reach carries `start` or `ask`.\\n\\n## 2. Planning trigger\\n\\n- Required: no. There is no active P0 and no active P1, so the promotion gate is PASS.\\n- Recommended: yes, as one small cleanup packet. Four of the seven advisories are one-line or\\n  one-sentence fixes, and two of them (the doc counts) are corrections to text added in this change.\\n- Not recommended: a remediation plan that reopens the command-surfacing design. The route-derived\\n  attach contract, the policy ladder and the single-mode rule are sound.\\n\\n## 3. Active finding registry\\n\\n| Id | Severity | Dimension | Location | Title |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| R1-P2-001 | P2 | correctness | `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:385` | Deep-loop depth gate is satisfied by any typed `/deep:` prefix, not the attached command |\\n| R1-P2-002 | P2 | correctness | `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:266` | Typed-command scan reads a document reference as the command |\\n| R2-P2-001 | P2 | security | `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:353` | Hub-attached commands skip the no-edit gate the command scorer applies |\\n| R3-P2-001 | P2 | traceability | `README.md:176` (also `feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md:26`) | Two docs added by this change state 45 TypeScript-served command rows; the artifact holds 46 |\\n| R3-P2-002 | P2 | traceability | `ARCHITECTURE.md:142` | The runtime coverage sentence omits `dsh` while the canonical set and hook readers include it |\\n| R4-P2-001 | P2 | maintainability | `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:123` | `COMMAND_POLICIES` is generated, drift-guarded and documented as the attach-path policy lookup, but no code reads it |\\n| R4-P2-002 | P2 | maintainability | `runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:750` | Dead empty conditional in `primaryIntentBonus` |\\n\\nTotals: P0 0, P1 0, P2 7 active, 0 resolved, 0 repeated.\\n\\n## 4. Remediation workstreams\\n\\n**W1 - Attach-path guards** (R1-P2-001, R1-P2-002, R2-P2-001)\\nReuse one predicate for \\\"the prompt asks for no change\\\" on the hub-attach path, the way\\n`fusion.ts` already does for command rows; match a typed command only at a command boundary that\\nrejects a trailing `.` path extension; and gate a deep-loop command on the command actually attached\\n(or on a per-command effort table) rather than on the presence of `/deep:`.\\nOwner: the advisor runtime. Size: one file plus tests. Risk: low — three narrow guards, all with a\\nunit reproduction already in the iteration files.\\n\\n**W2 - Documentation truth** (R3-P2-001, R3-P2-002)\\nCorrect the two 45-row sentences to 46 and add `dsh` to the runtime sentence (or state what the\\nsentence is enumerating if it is deliberately narrower than the runtime label set).\\nOwner: docs. Size: three lines. Risk: none.\\n\\n**W3 - Dead generated surface** (R4-P2-001)\\nChoose one: delete `COMMAND_POLICIES` from the generated block and its emitter, or point\\n`advisor-recommend.ts:478` at it and drop the duplicate policy from `TRACKED_COMMANDS`. The second is\\nthe smaller diff and makes the two prose surfaces agree. The `render-hooks-plugin` catalog page that\\nalready describes the second shape is another lineage's file, so a coordinated touch is needed if the\\ndelete option is chosen.\\nOwner: advisor runtime plus that doc's owner. Size: one emitter change and one consumer line, or a\\ndelete plus drift-guard update. Risk: low.\\n\\n**W4 - Dead control flow** (R4-P2-002)\\nDelete the empty `if` block in `primaryIntentBonus`. No expected-output change.\\nOwner: advisor runtime. Size: two lines. Risk: none.\\n\\n## 5. Spec seed\\n\\nProposed acceptance criteria for a cleanup packet:\\n\\n1. A prompt containing only `/deep:<other-mode>` never attaches a deep command for a different mode.\\n2. A prompt that cites a command document path (`/create:<name>.md`) attaches no command.\\n3. A prompt matching the shared no-edit wording attaches no mutating command from either the scorer\\n   path or the hub route path.\\n4. The documented TypeScript-served command-row count equals `counts.typescriptActive` in\\n   `command-bridges.generated.json`.\\n5. The architecture runtime sentence names every runtime in `ADVISOR_RUNTIME_VALUES`, or states the\\n   narrower enumeration it intends.\\n6. No generated export in `command-attach.ts` lacks a runtime consumer, or its documented consumer is\\n   the one that reads it.\\n7. The scoring path contains no empty conditional.\\n\\n## 6. Plan seed\\n\\n1. Add the no-edit predicate to `attachCommand` and reuse the same regex constant as `fusion.ts`\\n   (avoid a second copy).\\n2. Tighten `typedCommandIn`'s end boundary so a `.` or a path separator after the command cancels the\\n   match, keeping `-` as a continuation character.\\n3. Replace the `includes('/deep:')` bypass with a check on the command returned for the routed mode.\\n4. Update the two row-count sentences and the runtime sentence.\\n5. Resolve `COMMAND_POLICIES`: wire the consumer or delete the block and its emitter.\\n6. Delete the empty conditional.\\n7. Add one regression test per changed behaviour, each failing on the old code for exactly one reason.\\n\\n## 7. Traceability status\\n\\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Notes |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| `spec_code` | core | partial | Four P2 deviations across the generated tables and their docs. |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | partial | No packet checklist claim is contradicted; no claim covers the generated blocks. |\\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | pass | 36 doctor bridge owners match their 17 router `skill_agent` tags, 0 mismatches. |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | partial | Seven runtime labels accepted; architecture prose omits `dsh`. |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | partial | Cosine 0.72 and margin 0.02 claims match the constants; the 45-row count does not. |\\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | notApplicable | No playbook path in this surface. |\\n\\nResource Map Coverage Gate: skipped — no `resource-map.md` at init.\\n\\n## 8. Deferred items\\n\\n- Holdout-path hygiene for the `tune`, `fix` and report commands: the implementations live in\\n  `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/*` and belong to the `accuracy-runner` lineage. This lineage\\n  verified only that its own surface never reads or prints holdout rows, and read no holdout prompt\\n  text (counts only).\\n- Compiled-route mode selection for no-edit prompts: proving the reach of R2-P2-001 needs a write-safe\\n  probe of `.skilled/bin/compiled-route.cjs --hub sk-doc`, which is outside this lineage's write-safe\\n  scope.\\n- The `feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md` sentence that names `COMMAND_POLICIES` as the\\n  policy source: `render-hooks-plugin` owns that file; it was cited as context for R4-P2-001 and not\\n  filed against.\\n- Runtime-specific command rendering (the hook brief and the six runtime adapters): outside this\\n  lineage; the runtime label set and the docs were checked, the renderers were not.\\n\\n## 9. Audit appendix\\n\\n- Iterations: `iterations/iteration-001.md` … `iteration-005.md`; deltas `deltas/iter-001.jsonl` …\\n  `iter-005.jsonl`; each iteration recorded once through `append-mode-event.cjs` (ledger sequences\\n  2-6, all exit 0) and reduced with `reduce-state.cjs`.\\n- Evidence style: every finding cites `file:line`. Four findings were reproduced by executing the\\n  shipped module with `node --experimental-strip-types`; four whole-table checks were executed\\n  (`COMMAND_ROWS` policy/class sweep, policy-map agreement, `MODE_COMMANDS` file existence, doctor\\n  owner tags).\\n- Scope audit: every write resolved under\\n  `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach`.\\n  No review target, config, findings registry, dashboard, command, skill or mirror was hand-edited;\\n  the registry and dashboard are reducer output.\\n- Anti-sycophancy note: R2-P2-001 was tested against its own P1 promotion trigger in iteration 5 and\\n  held at P2 because the reach condition was not proven.\\n- Holdout handling: no holdout prompt text was read or printed in any iteration.\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach/review-report.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794552001096,"end":1794552033236}}}}
